2026-06-08 17:21:13,520 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780935673520442","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"bfc147c357a9863316134f1c6c8717dc","trajectoryId":"bfc147c357a9863316134f1c6c8717dc","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\nSystem design, architecture decisions, and ADR drafting. Write to docs/architecture/ only. Do not write implementation code.\n\nSPECIFIC DESIGN RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. LSTM-VAE Architecture Specification (Input shape: (batch, seq_len=20, input_dim=4), Encoder hidden sizes: [64, 32], 8D latent space).\n2. Loss: MSE reconstruction + KL divergence with beta=0.1.\n3. Latent reparameterization z = mu + std * epsilon.\n4. Design documentation under docs/architecture/lstm_vae_design.md.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: CODE REVIEW CHECKLIST\n# Code Review Skill\nskill_id: \"code-review\"\nname: \"Code Review\"\ndescription: \"Capability to review code for quality, architecture, and best practices\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\nchecklist:\n  quality:\n    - \"Code follows project style guide\"\n    - \"Proper error handling\"\n    - \"No code duplication\"\n    - \"Proper logging\"\n\n  testing:\n    - \"Tests provided\"\n    - \"Test coverage >80%\"\n    - \"Edge cases handled\"\n    - \"All tests passing\"\n\n  documentation:\n    - \"Docstrings complete\"\n    - \"Type hints present\"\n    - \"README updated\"\n    - \"Examples provided\"\n\n  architecture:\n    - \"No tight coupling\"\n    - \"Components independent\"\n    - \"Scalable design\"\n    - \"Extensible for Phase 1.5\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Passes [category]\"\n  - \"⚠️  Warning: [issue]\"\n  - \"🛑 Blocker: [issue]\"\n  - \"📝 Recommendation: [suggestion]\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEKLY-SYNC-CONTEXT)\n# Weekly Sync Context Handover\nhandover_id: \"weekly-sync\"\nname: \"Weekly Sync Context\"\ndescription: \"Passing context from one week to agents for next week\"\n\ntrigger: \"Friday end of week\"\n\ntemplate: |\n  Team sync context:\n\n  Week [N] Progress:\n  - ML Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - Backend Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - DevOps Lead: [What was accomplished]\n  - Architect: [Assessment of week]\n\n  Metrics:\n  - Model accuracy: [X]%\n  - API latency: [X]ms\n  - Test coverage: [X]%\n  - Infrastructure status: [Status]\n\n  Blockers:\n  - [Blocker 1]\n  - [Blocker 2]\n\n  Week [N+1] Focus:\n  - ML Engineer will: [Task]\n  - Backend Engineer will: [Task]\n  - DevOps Lead will: [Task]\n  - Architect will: [Task]\n\n  Questions for next week:\n  - [Question 1]\n  - [Question 2]\n\nagents_to_receive:\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\ntiming: \"Monday morning before work starts\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Review the Week 1 foundation architecture (LSTM-VAE, training pipeline, tests, Docker) and answer the 'Architecture Assessment Questions' from the prompt. The components to review are: src/models/lstm_vae.py, src/models/data_generator.py, src/models/training.py, tests/unit/, docker-compose.yml, and Dockerfile. Create a markdown file with your findings.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\nSystem design, architecture decisions, and ADR drafting. Write to docs/architecture/ only. Do not write implementation code.\n\nSPECIFIC DESIGN RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. LSTM-VAE Architecture Specification (Input shape: (batch, seq_len=20, input_dim=4), Encoder hidden sizes: [64, 32], 8D latent space).\n2. Loss: MSE reconstruction + KL divergence with beta=0.1.\n3. Latent reparameterization z = mu + std * epsilon.\n4. Design documentation under docs/architecture/lstm_vae_design.md.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: CODE REVIEW CHECKLIST\n# Code Review Skill\nskill_id: \"code-review\"\nname: \"Code Review\"\ndescription: \"Capability to review code for quality, architecture, and best practices\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\nchecklist:\n  quality:\n    - \"Code follows project style guide\"\n    - \"Proper error handling\"\n    - \"No code duplication\"\n    - \"Proper logging\"\n\n  testing:\n    - \"Tests provided\"\n    - \"Test coverage >80%\"\n    - \"Edge cases handled\"\n    - \"All tests passing\"\n\n  documentation:\n    - \"Docstrings complete\"\n    - \"Type hints present\"\n    - \"README updated\"\n    - \"Examples provided\"\n\n  architecture:\n    - \"No tight coupling\"\n    - \"Components independent\"\n    - \"Scalable design\"\n    - \"Extensible for Phase 1.5\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Passes [category]\"\n  - \"⚠️  Warning: [issue]\"\n  - \"🛑 Blocker: [issue]\"\n  - \"📝 Recommendation: [suggestion]\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEKLY-SYNC-CONTEXT)\n# Weekly Sync Context Handover\nhandover_id: \"weekly-sync\"\nname: \"Weekly Sync Context\"\ndescription: \"Passing context from one week to agents for next week\"\n\ntrigger: \"Friday end of week\"\n\ntemplate: |\n  Team sync context:\n\n  Week [N] Progress:\n  - ML Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - Backend Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - DevOps Lead: [What was accomplished]\n  - Architect: [Assessment of week]\n\n  Metrics:\n  - Model accuracy: [X]%\n  - API latency: [X]ms\n  - Test coverage: [X]%\n  - Infrastructure status: [Status]\n\n  Blockers:\n  - [Blocker 1]\n  - [Blocker 2]\n\n  Week [N+1] Focus:\n  - ML Engineer will: [Task]\n  - Backend Engineer will: [Task]\n  - DevOps Lead will: [Task]\n  - Architect will: [Task]\n\n  Questions for next week:\n  - [Question 1]\n  - [Question 2]\n\nagents_to_receive:\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\ntiming: \"Monday morning before work starts\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Review the Week 1 foundation architecture (LSTM-VAE, training pipeline, tests, Docker) and answer the 'Architecture Assessment Questions' from the prompt. The components to review are: src/models/lstm_vae.py, src/models/data_generator.py, src/models/training.py, tests/unit/, docker-compose.yml, and Dockerfile. Create a markdown file with your findings.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
