2026-06-08 17:32:11,260 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780936331260382","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"22d3f9b887a395d5eb056b3e6a50ff9c","trajectoryId":"22d3f9b887a395d5eb056b3e6a50ff9c","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\npytest test suites, integration tests, coverage enforcement. Target 90% coverage. Write to tests/ only. Never modify implementation files.\n\nSPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Create tests/unit/test_lstm_vae.py.\n2. Create tests/unit/test_data_generator.py.\n3. Create tests/integration/test_model_training.py.\n4. Configure pytest.ini and .coveragerc.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: AUTOMATED TESTING GATE\n# Automated Testing Skill\nskill_id: \"automated-testing\"\nname: \"Automated Testing\"\ndescription: \"Capability to implement robust unit and integration tests and verify coverage gates\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"qa-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n\nchecklist:\n  unit_tests:\n    - \"Test files are located under tests/unit/ and start with test_\"\n    - \"Verify input and output tensor shapes on all key model layers\"\n    - \"Test mathematical stability (check that loss is positive, non-NaN, non-Inf)\"\n    - \"Test model reparameterization trick for correct stochastic behavior\"\n    - \"Test model checkpoint saving and loading metadata (epoch, loss, accuracy, config)\"\n    - \"Test reproducibility with fixed random seed constraints\"\n\n  integration_tests:\n    - \"Integration test files are located under tests/integration/\"\n    - \"Verify end-to-end model training runs and successfully reduces loss over epochs\"\n    - \"Verify early stopping triggers correctly when loss plateaus\"\n    - \"Verify data generation produces correct shape, bounds [0, 1], and correlations\"\n\n  coverage:\n    - \"Coverage configuration is maintained in .coveragerc\"\n    - \"pytest.ini defines term-missing and cov-fail-under=80\"\n    - \"Critical paths (model forward, loss calculation, training loop) target >90% coverage\"\n    - \"Ensure coverage stays above the 80.0% global gate\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Test Passed: [test name]\"\n  - \"❌ Test Failed: [issue details]\"\n  - \"📊 Coverage Status: [X]% (Target: >80%)\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Provide feedback on code quality (Type Hints, Documentation, Error Handling, Testing, Code Organization, Reproducibility) and provide recommendations for Phase 2 (Things to Keep, Things to Improve, Phase 2 Extensions).\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: CODE_QUALITY_AND_PHASE_2_RECOMMENDATIONS.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\npytest test suites, integration tests, coverage enforcement. Target 90% coverage. Write to tests/ only. Never modify implementation files.\n\nSPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Create tests/unit/test_lstm_vae.py.\n2. Create tests/unit/test_data_generator.py.\n3. Create tests/integration/test_model_training.py.\n4. Configure pytest.ini and .coveragerc.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: AUTOMATED TESTING GATE\n# Automated Testing Skill\nskill_id: \"automated-testing\"\nname: \"Automated Testing\"\ndescription: \"Capability to implement robust unit and integration tests and verify coverage gates\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"qa-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n\nchecklist:\n  unit_tests:\n    - \"Test files are located under tests/unit/ and start with test_\"\n    - \"Verify input and output tensor shapes on all key model layers\"\n    - \"Test mathematical stability (check that loss is positive, non-NaN, non-Inf)\"\n    - \"Test model reparameterization trick for correct stochastic behavior\"\n    - \"Test model checkpoint saving and loading metadata (epoch, loss, accuracy, config)\"\n    - \"Test reproducibility with fixed random seed constraints\"\n\n  integration_tests:\n    - \"Integration test files are located under tests/integration/\"\n    - \"Verify end-to-end model training runs and successfully reduces loss over epochs\"\n    - \"Verify early stopping triggers correctly when loss plateaus\"\n    - \"Verify data generation produces correct shape, bounds [0, 1], and correlations\"\n\n  coverage:\n    - \"Coverage configuration is maintained in .coveragerc\"\n    - \"pytest.ini defines term-missing and cov-fail-under=80\"\n    - \"Critical paths (model forward, loss calculation, training loop) target >90% coverage\"\n    - \"Ensure coverage stays above the 80.0% global gate\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Test Passed: [test name]\"\n  - \"❌ Test Failed: [issue details]\"\n  - \"📊 Coverage Status: [X]% (Target: >80%)\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Provide feedback on code quality (Type Hints, Documentation, Error Handling, Testing, Code Organization, Reproducibility) and provide recommendations for Phase 2 (Things to Keep, Things to Improve, Phase 2 Extensions).\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: CODE_QUALITY_AND_PHASE_2_RECOMMENDATIONS.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
