onsidering the output and context from previous agents. I'm focusing on making file creation the responsibility of the final phase.\n\n\n**Refining the Integration Focus**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the integration, given that the plan is almost complete. My focus will be on ensuring the architecture and review content is combined. I'm focusing on the plan to combine the file.\n\n\n\n**Orchestrating the Architecture Review**\n\nI'm now prioritizing clarity. Considering the parallel nature implied by the user's syntax `@architect @code-reviewer`, I'll structure the execution in phases. I am confident in the flow now.\n\n\n**Refining the Final Plan**\n\nI'm now implementing the final parallel plan, translating the detailed user request into actionable tasks for the agents. The focus remains on clear separation of concerns: the architect handling architecture and ADRs, the code reviewer focusing on code quality, and a tech-lead integrating the content. I am finalizing the `finish` call.\n\n```python\n# The full user request as  a variable\nuser_request = \"\"\"\n# 📋 TASK 5: Architecture Review & ADR Documentation\n## Friday Morning  - Stage 1 (Gemma Code Generation)\n...\n\"\"\"\n\n# Phase 1\nphase1 = {\n    \"phase\": 1,\n    \"parallel\": True,\n    \"agents\": [\n        {\n             \"agent\": \"architect\",\n            \"task\": f\"As the Architect, your task is to analyze the provided prompt and generate the required architecture documents.\\n- Perform the 'Architecture Review' (Section 1).\\n- Generate the content for the three 'Architecture Decision Records' (Section 2).\\n- Provide 'Recommendations for Phase 2' (Section 4).\\n**DO NOT** perform the 'Code Quality Assessment' (Section 3).\\nCombine all outputs into a single markdown file using the original headings from the prompt.\\n\\n---\\nFULL USER REQUEST:\\n{user_request}\",\n            \"output_file\": \"architect_review.md\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"agent\": \"code-reviewer\",\n            \"task\": f\"As the Code Reviewer, your task is to analyze the provided prompt and assess the code quality.\\n- Perform ONLY the 'Code Quality Assessment' (Section 3).\\n- Your output should be a markdown document covering all points in that section.\\n**DO NOT** perform any other sections of the review (1, 2, or 4).\\n\\n---\\nFULL USER REQUEST:\\n{user_request}\",\n            \"output_file\": \"code_quality_assessment.md\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n# Phase 2\nphase2 = {\n    \"phase\": 2,\n    \"agents\": [\n        {\n            \"agent\": \"tech-lead\",\n            \"task\": \"As the Tech Lead integrator, your task is to process the files from the 'architect' and 'code-reviewer' to finalize the documentation.\\n- From the architect's output file, extract the content for the three ADRs.\\n- Create the final ADR files in `docs/team/ADRs/`, named as specified in the original prompt (e.g., `ADR-001-lstm-vae-architecture.md`).\\n- Combine the 'Architecture Assessment' and 'Phase 2 Recommendations' from the architect's file with the 'Code Quality Assessment' from the code-reviewer's file into a single `ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md` file.\\n- Report completion status.\",\n            \"context_from\": [\"architect_review.md\", \"code_quality_assessment.md\"],\n            \"output_file\": \"integration_summary.md\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n# Final plan\nplan = [phase1, phase2]\n\n# Call the finish tool\n# Assuming there is a finish tool and it takes this JSON plan\n# finish(plan)\n```\n\nNow, I am confident in the plan. The key is now ensuring that this plan executes correctly, given the structure of the prompt.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Phase 1 Analysis**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a clear sequence. The initial stage involves both the 'architect' and 'code-reviewer,' as the user directed.  I will have the architect focus on architecture review and ADRs, with the reviewer assessing the code. This will feed into a second stage, handled by the integrator for final file creation.