ame intermediate file and provide overall comments.\n\n\n\n**Orchestrating Workflow Refinement**\n\nI've revised the agent workflow for a clearer structure, with agents now generating markdown files. The `architect` will first focus on producing an `ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md` file, which includes architectural assessment. The architect will also draft the content for the ADRs. I will then utilize the `backend-engineer` to finalize these into the actual ADR files in parallel, and finally use the `code-reviewer` to complete the process.\n\n\n**Refining Agent Outputs**\n\nI am now structuring the output to ensure each agent generates a single file, as instructed. The architect will produce `ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md`, `ADR-001`, `ADR-002`, and `ADR-003` files. The code reviewer will then review these files, and will provide an overall review summary and recommendations for any required revisions, creating `final_architecture_review.md`. I have updated the task specifications for each agent accordingly.\n\n\n**Refining Plan Refinement**\n\nI've significantly restructured the workflow to align with a more granular, single-file output strategy for each agent. This revised approach enhances task focus and simplifies the integration of outputs. I am now planning to create and integrate the final ADR and assessment documents. The next step is drafting the new, focused prompts, and testing them using a dry-run.\n\n\n**Refining Agent Prompts**\n\nI've crafted and refined the task prompts for each agent, focusing on clear instructions and single-file outputs, in alignment with user specifications. The \"architect\" now has separate tasks to assess the architecture and draft individual ADRs, each targeting a specific output file. I've ensured all instructions are incorporated, including the detailed questions and templates provided by the user. The `code-reviewer` agent gets the last stage.\n\n\n**Refining Agent Tasks**\n\nMy plan is now to use a set of focused, single-output tasks for the architect. The architect will produce the architecture assessment and individual ADRs, and a code reviewer will then check and finalize all outputs. I'm aiming for structured workflows. I am creating a \"review\" phase.\n\n\n```python\n**Refining Plan Implementation**\n\nI've finalized the implementation plan, ensuring granular tasks with single-file outputs, in line with the revised requirements. I'm now structuring the `finish` call, incorporating the full user prompt as context for each agent, enhancing their task comprehension and ensuring compliance with all constraints. I will ensure the execution adheres to the phased plan.\n```\n\n\nI'm working on refining the plan, now focusing on granular tasks and single-file outputs for each agent, enhancing focus and simplicity. I've drafted prompts to direct the architect to create each file, and then the `code-reviewer` to consolidate the work. The full prompt is included with each task.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Workflow**\n\nI'm now implementing the multi-agent workflow for the `ai-agronomist` architecture review. I've broken the task into phases: architect, architect-draft ADRs, and final code review. The plan involves granular steps and single-file outputs, in line with the user requirements. I am crafting detailed prompts for each phase.\n\n\n","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"**Orchestrating Workflow**\n\nI'm now implementing the multi-agent workflow for the `ai-agronomist` architecture review. I've broken the task into phases: architect, architect-draft ADRs, and final code review. The plan involves granular steps and single-file outputs, in line with the user requirements. I am crafting detailed prompts for each phase.\n\n\n","text":""}}
