2026-06-08 18:11:03,296 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"24","timestampMicros":"1780938663296473","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"f83250ac3c4612479bc683470647df18","trajectoryId":"f83250ac3c4612479bc683470647df18","stepIndex":8,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Overwrite ADR-003 documentation","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-phase-1-5-architecture.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":54,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-003: Modular Architecture for Phase 1.5","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Status**: Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Date**: 2026-06-08","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Architect**: Agent, Antigravity","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Stakeholders**: ML Engineer, Backend Engineer, DevOps Lead","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"# ADR-003: Modular Architecture for Easy Phase 1.5 Scaling","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Status","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"ACCEPTED","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"Phase 1 of the AI Agronomist platform established a monolithic architecture for initial setup and deployment. As we approach Phase 1.5, which will introduce new sensor types (e.g., pH, EC), a soil moisture model, and customer-specific alerting, the monolithic approach will become a bottleneck. It hinders independent development, testing, and deployment, and makes technology stack upgrades difficult.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"This ADR proposes a shift to a modular, service-oriented architecture to address these challenges and prepare for future scalability.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"Phase 1: Single model, single customer","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Phase 1.5: Model adaptation infrastructure, 3-5 customers with different crops/conditions","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Phase 2: Multi-customer platform with vendor integration","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Must design Phase 1 to avoid major refactoring at Phase 1.5.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Problem","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"How to structure Phase 1 code to enable Phase 1.5 multi-customer scaling?","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"We will adopt a modular architecture composed of four distinct services:","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"1.  **Ingestion Service**: Handles data intake from all sensor types. It will be responsible for authentication, protocol translation (e.g., MQTT, HTTP), and publishing raw data to a central message queue.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"2.  **Processing Service**: Consumes data from the message queue, enriches it with metadata, and runs it through the appropriate anomaly detection models (initially, the LSTM-VAE). It will also be responsible for storing the results.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"3.  **API Service**: Exposes a RESTful API for fetching processed data, model insights, and managing configurations. This service will be the primary interface for the frontend application.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"4.  **Alerting Service**: Monitors for anomalies and triggers alerts based on user-defined rules. This service will be responsible for sending notifications via various channels (e.g., email, SMS).","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"These services will communicate asynchronously via a message queue (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka) to ensure loose coupling and resilience. Each service will have its own database to enforce clear data ownership and domain boundaries.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"Three design principles:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"1. **Separated Concerns**","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Models (src/models/) independent of data/API","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Data loading (src/data/) independent of model","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Database (Phase 2) independent of model","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"2. **Configuration-Driven**","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - No hardcoded paths, hyperparameters in config.py","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Easy to adjust for different greenhouse types","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Environment variables for deployment flexibility","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"3. **Pluggable Components**","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Data generator can be swapped for real data loader (Phase 1.5)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Training script can handle multiple models (Phase 1.5)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"   - Database schema extensible (Phase 2 additions)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Rationale","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"This modular approach offers several key advantages:","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Scalability**: Each service can be scaled independently based on its specific load.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Extensibility**: New features, such as additional sensor types or models, can be added as new services without impacting existing ones.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Technology Freedom**: Each service can be built with the most appropriate technology stack, allowing for greater flexibility and optimization.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Developer Autonomy**: Teams can develop, test, and deploy their services independently, accelerating the development lifecycle.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Resilience**: The failure of one service will not cascade and bring down the entire system, thanks to asynchronous communication.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"1. **Minimal Refactoring**: <20% of Phase 1 work at Phase 1.5","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"2. **Reusability**: Base model can transfer to new customers","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"3. **Testability**: Each component independently testable","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"4. **Maintainability**: Clear interfaces between components","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Increased Complexity**: The initial setup will be more complex, requiring a robust CI/CD pipeline, container orchestration (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes), and a centralized logging/monitoring solution.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Data Consistency**: Maintaining data consistency across services will require careful design, potentially using patterns like the Saga pattern for distributed transactions.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Inter-service Communication**: Secure and reliable communication between services must be established, including robust error handling and retry mechanisms.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **DevOps Overhead**: The DevOps team will need to manage a more complex infrastructure, including the deployment and monitoring of multiple services.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"## Implementation Plan","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"1.  **ADR Approval**: Finalize and approve this ADR with all stakeholders.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"2.  **Technology Selection**: Choose the specific technologies for the message queue, databases, and container orchestration.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"3.  **Service Scaffolding**: Create the initial repository structure and CI/CD pipelines for each service.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"4.  **Phase 1 Migration**:","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"    - Decompose the existing monolith into the four defined services.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"    - Prioritize the Ingestion and Processing services to ensure data continuity.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"    - Develop the API and Alerting services in parallel.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"5.  **Testing**: Implement comprehensive integration tests to ensure seamless communication and data flow between services.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"6.  **Deployment**: Deploy the new architecture to a staging environment for thorough testing before a phased rollout to production.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"This modular architecture will provide the AI Agronomist platform with the solid foundation needed for sustainable growth and rapid innovation.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- Slightly more abstraction than needed for Phase 1","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- More files/classes (vs monolithic script)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- Configuration management overhead (mitigated by defaults)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Code Structure","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"src/","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"├── models/           # Model definitions (same for all customers)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   ├── lstm_vae.py","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   ├── data_generator.py  # Swappable with real loader","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   └── training.py","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"├── data/             # Data loading (will expand Phase 1.5)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   └── csv_loader.py","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"└── config.py         # All hardcoded values here","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Phase 1.5 additions:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"├── data/","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   ├── priva_loader.py         # NEW: Priva API integration","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   └── greenhouse_adapter.py    # NEW: Vendor-agnostic adapter","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"├── models/","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"│   └── model_adapter.py         # NEW: Transfer learning","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"└── database/         # NEW: Customer data storage","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Phase 1.5 Refactoring Budget","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- Data loading: 30% new code, 0% existing code changes","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- Model adaptation: 20% new code, 5% existing code changes","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- Database layer: 50% new code, 0% existing code changes","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- Total: ~<20% effort relative to Phase 1","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"}]}]}}}
