2026-06-08 18:11:50,535 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780938710535674","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"463cee63618aba2c9ed1d1317e46ac5a","trajectoryId":"463cee63618aba2c9ed1d1317e46ac5a","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== architect output ===\n# ADR-003: Modular Architecture for Easy Phase 1.5 Scaling\n\n## Status\n\nACCEPTED\n\n## Context\n\nPhase 1: Single model, single customer\nPhase 1.5: Model adaptation infrastructure, 3-5 customers with different crops/conditions\nPhase 2: Multi-customer platform with vendor integration\n\nMust design Phase 1 to avoid major refactoring at Phase 1.5.\n\n## Problem\n\nHow to structure Phase 1 code to enable Phase 1.5 multi-customer scaling?\n\n## Decision\n\nThree design principles:\n\n1. **Separated Concerns**\n   - Models (src/models/) independent of data/API\n   - Data loading (src/data/) independent of model\n   - Database (Phase 2) independent of model\n\n2. **Configuration-Driven**\n   - No hardcoded paths, hyperparameters in config.py\n   - Easy to adjust for different greenhouse types\n   - Environment variables for deployment flexibility\n\n3. **Pluggable Components**\n   - Data generator can be swapped for real data loader (Phase 1.5)\n   - Training script can handle multiple models (Phase 1.5)\n   - Database schema extensible (Phase 2 additions)\n\n## Rationale\n\n1. **Minimal Refactoring**: <20% of Phase 1 work at Phase 1.5\n2. **Reusability**: Base model can transfer to new customers\n3. **Testability**: Each component independently testable\n4. **Maintainability**: Clear interfaces between components\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Slightly more abstraction than needed for Phase 1\n- More files/classes (vs monolithic script)\n- Configuration management overhead (mitigated by defaults)\n\n## Code Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── models/           # Model definitions (same for all customers)\n│   ├── lstm_vae.py\n│   ├── data_generator.py  # Swappable with real loader\n│   └── training.py\n├── data/             # Data loading (will expand Phase 1.5)\n│   └── csv_loader.py\n└── config.py         # All hardcoded values here\n\nPhase 1.5 additions:\n├── data/\n│   ├── priva_loader.py         # NEW: Priva API integration\n│   └── greenhouse_adapter.py    # NEW: Vendor-agnostic adapter\n├── models/\n│   └── model_adapter.py         # NEW: Transfer learning\n└── database/         # NEW: Customer data storage\n```\n\n## Phase 1.5 Refactoring Budget\n\n- Data loading: 30% new code, 0% existing code changes\n- Model adaptation: 20% new code, 5% existing code changes\n- Database layer: 50% new code, 0% existing code changes\n- Total: ~<20% effort relative to Phase 1\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review the generated ADRs and the architecture assessment for clarity, correctness, and completeness.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: docs/team/ADRs/REVIEW.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== architect output ===\n# ADR-003: Modular Architecture for Easy Phase 1.5 Scaling\n\n## Status\n\nACCEPTED\n\n## Context\n\nPhase 1: Single model, single customer\nPhase 1.5: Model adaptation infrastructure, 3-5 customers with different crops/conditions\nPhase 2: Multi-customer platform with vendor integration\n\nMust design Phase 1 to avoid major refactoring at Phase 1.5.\n\n## Problem\n\nHow to structure Phase 1 code to enable Phase 1.5 multi-customer scaling?\n\n## Decision\n\nThree design principles:\n\n1. **Separated Concerns**\n   - Models (src/models/) independent of data/API\n   - Data loading (src/data/) independent of model\n   - Database (Phase 2) independent of model\n\n2. **Configuration-Driven**\n   - No hardcoded paths, hyperparameters in config.py\n   - Easy to adjust for different greenhouse types\n   - Environment variables for deployment flexibility\n\n3. **Pluggable Components**\n   - Data generator can be swapped for real data loader (Phase 1.5)\n   - Training script can handle multiple models (Phase 1.5)\n   - Database schema extensible (Phase 2 additions)\n\n## Rationale\n\n1. **Minimal Refactoring**: <20% of Phase 1 work at Phase 1.5\n2. **Reusability**: Base model can transfer to new customers\n3. **Testability**: Each component independently testable\n4. **Maintainability**: Clear interfaces between components\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Slightly more abstraction than needed for Phase 1\n- More files/classes (vs monolithic script)\n- Configuration management overhead (mitigated by defaults)\n\n## Code Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── models/           # Model definitions (same for all customers)\n│   ├── lstm_vae.py\n│   ├── data_generator.py  # Swappable with real loader\n│   └── training.py\n├── data/             # Data loading (will expand Phase 1.5)\n│   └── csv_loader.py\n└── config.py         # All hardcoded values here\n\nPhase 1.5 additions:\n├── data/\n│   ├── priva_loader.py         # NEW: Priva API integration\n│   └── greenhouse_adapter.py    # NEW: Vendor-agnostic adapter\n├── models/\n│   └── model_adapter.py         # NEW: Transfer learning\n└── database/         # NEW: Customer data storage\n```\n\n## Phase 1.5 Refactoring Budget\n\n- Data loading: 30% new code, 0% existing code changes\n- Model adaptation: 20% new code, 5% existing code changes\n- Database layer: 50% new code, 0% existing code changes\n- Total: ~<20% effort relative to Phase 1\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review the generated ADRs and the architecture assessment for clarity, correctness, and completeness.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: docs/team/ADRs/REVIEW.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
