2026-06-08 18:32:02,316 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"20","timestampMicros":"1780939922313422","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"11cbe34e2b83313db8305d5b2333daec","trajectoryId":"11cbe34e2b83313db8305d5b2333daec","stepIndex":2,"state":"STATE_WAITING_FOR_USER","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_USER","thinking":"","textDelta":"Finished","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Finished","finish":{"outputString":"{\"phases\":[{\"agents\":[{\"agent\":\"architect\",\"output_file\":\"docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md\",\"task\":\"Design the REST API, Streamlit dashboard, and vendor adapter architecture, producing two design documents. The first document, to be saved as docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md, will detail REST API endpoint specifications (including GET /health, GET /health/db, POST /api/upload, and POST /api/inference), request/response schemas for each endpoint, a comprehensive error handling strategy for validation and server errors, and a rate limiting strategy in preparation for multi-customer support. Additionally, it will outline the Streamlit dashboard's page specifications for sensor_data.py, anomalies.py, thresholds.py, and metrics.py, covering state management with session state and caching, a real-time refresh strategy, a multi-tenant filtering UI, and the threshold adjustment flow. The document will also include a high-level database schema, specifying the SensorReading table structure, necessary indexes, and support for multi-tenancy with a tenant_id.\"},{\"agent\":\"architect\",\"output_file\":\"docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md\",\"task\":\"Produce the second design document, docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md, which will define the abstract vendor interface specification, including the methods each adapter must implement, their input/output contracts, and error handling on a per-vendor basis. The document will also detail the current CSV adapter implementation, a stub for the Priva adapter for future implementation, a data normalization layer to standardize data from different vendors, and a discussion on future extensibility for integrating other potential vendors.\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/api/main.py\",\"task\":\"Implement the initial FastAPI application structure in src/api/main.py, including the FastAPI() app instantiation, CORS middleware configured to allow localhost access for Streamlit, dependency injection for database sessions, and global exception handlers for 422, 404, and 500 errors. Also, implement a startup hook to initialize the database and a shutdown hook for resource cleanup, and add request ID middleware for logging purposes.\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/db/models.py\",\"task\":\"Create the SQLAlchemy ORM model for SensorReading in src/db/models.py, with fields for id, tenant_id, greenhouse_id, timestamp, temperature, humidity, co2, light, an optional anomaly_score, and a created_at timestamp. Ensure that tenant_id and timestamp are indexed, and set up the base class for all models to enable table creation via SQLAlchemy declarative.\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/api/schemas/sensor_data.py\",\"task\":\"Implement Pydantic v2 models in src/api/schemas/sensor_data.py for SensorReadingCreate, SensorReadingResponse, UploadRequest, UploadResponse, InferenceRequest, and InferenceResponse, ensuring that all models include type hints and docstrings.\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/db/migrations/env.py\",\"task\":\"Set up Alembic for database migrations by initializing it and configuring the env.py file in src/db/migrations/ to use the SQLAlchemy models, preparing for auto-generating migrations.\"},{\"agent\":\"ml-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/models/inference.py\",\"task\":\"Enhance the AnomalyDetector class in src/models/inference.py by implementing methods for loading a trained LSTM-VAE model from a checkpoint, predicting anomaly scores from a batch of sequences, handling variable-length batches, and calculating reconstruction error. Also, add in-memory model caching and robust error handling for cases like a missing model, invalid input shapes, and NaN/Inf values in the output.\"},{\"agent\":\"ml-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/vendors/base.py\",\"task\":\"Create an abstract base class named DataSourceAdapter in src/vendors/base.py, defining methods for reading, normalizing, and validating data from various sources, and outline a per-vendor error handling strategy.\"},{\"agent\":\"ml-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/vendors/csv_adapter.py\",\"task\":\"Implement the CSVAdapter class in src/vendors/csv_adapter.py, inheriting from DataSourceAdapter, to handle reading data from CSV files, validating the required columns and data types, and normalizing the data using configured ranges.\"},{\"agent\":\"devops-lead\",\"output_file\":\"src/logging/config.py\",\"task\":\"Set up a structured logging configuration in src/logging/config.py, ensuring that the output format is JSON, with support for various log levels, daily log file rotation, and redaction of sensitive fields. Provide an example log entry to illustrate the desired format.\"},{\"agent\":\"devops-lead\",\"output_file\":\"src/api/middleware/logging.py\",\"task\":\"Implement FastAPI middleware for request/response logging in src/api/middleware/logging.py, capturing request method, path, and headers, as well as response status code, duration, and size, while propagating a request ID through the logs.\"},{\"agent\":\"devops-lead\",\"output_file\":\"pyproject.toml\",\"task\":\"Update the pyproject.toml file to include and pin the structlog and python-json-logger dependencies, and ensure that all other project dependencies are also pinned to specific versions.\"}],\"phase\":1}]}"},"requestText":"Requesting permission to make tool call","toolConfirmationRequest":{}}}
