odel input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEKLY-SYNC-CONTEXT)\n# Weekly Sync Context Handover\nhandover_id: \"weekly-sync\"\nname: \"Weekly Sync Context\"\ndescription: \"Passing context from one week to agents for next week\"\n\ntrigger: \"Friday end of week\"\n\ntemplate: |\n  Team sync context:\n\n  Week [N] Progress:\n  - ML Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - Backend Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - DevOps Lead: [What was accomplished]\n  - Architect: [Assessment of week]\n\n  Metrics:\n  - Model accuracy: [X]%\n  - API latency: [X]ms\n  - Test coverage: [X]%\n  - Infrastructure status: [Status]\n\n  Blockers:\n  - [Blocker 1]\n  - [Blocker 2]\n\n  Week [N+1] Focus:\n  - ML Engineer will: [Task]\n  - Backend Engineer will: [Task]\n  - DevOps Lead will: [Task]\n  - Architect will: [Task]\n\n  Questions for next week:\n  - [Question 1]\n  - [Question 2]\n\nagents_to_receive:\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\ntiming: \"Monday morning before work starts\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Design the REST API, Streamlit dashboard, and vendor adapter architecture, producing two design documents. The first document, to be saved as docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md, will detail REST API endpoint specifications (including GET /health, GET /health/db, POST /api/upload, and POST /api/inference), request/response schemas for each endpoint, a comprehensive error handling strategy for validation and server errors, and a rate limiting strategy in preparation for multi-customer support. Additionally, it will outline the Streamlit dashboard's page specifications for sensor_data.py, anomalies.py, thresholds.py, and metrics.py, covering state management with session state and caching, a rea