 data, anomaly detection. Write to src/models/ and src/config.py only.\n\nSPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Create LSTMVAE class in src/models/lstm_vae.py.\n2. Create SyntheticDataGenerator in src/models/data_generator.py.\n3. Create central src/config.py.\n4. Create VAETrainer and CheckpointManager in src/models/training.py and scripts/train_lstm_vae.py.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\nML SPECIFIC GUARDRAILS:\n# ML Guardrails\n\n## LSTM-VAE spec (locked — do not change without ADR)\nLSTMVAE(input_dim=4, hidden_dims=[64,32], latent_dim=8, seq_len=20, beta=0.1, dropout=0.2)\nLoss: MSE(x, x_recon) + beta * KL(N(μ,σ²) || N(0,I))\nLatent: z = μ + σ ⊙ ε, ε ~ N(0,I)\n\n## Sensor ranges (physical units)\n- Temperature: 20–30°C\n- Humidity: 50–80%\n- CO2: 300–500 ppm\n- Light: 0–1000 lux\n\n## STOP WORK\n- Checkpoint without: epoch, loss, accuracy, timestamp, model_config\n- NaN/Inf in model outputs with no detection\n- Training loop with no early stopping\n- Hard-coded sensor ranges (must reference src/config.py)\n\n## WARN\n- Beta > 1.0 (risk of posterior collapse)\n- Dropout > 0.5 (too aggressive)\n- Learning rate > 1e-2 (unstable)\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: CODE REVIEW CHECKLIST\n# Code Review Skill\nskill_id: \"code-review\"\nname: \"Code Review\"\ndescription: \"Capability to review code for quality, architecture, and best practices\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\nchecklist:\n  quality:\n    - \"Code follows project style guide\"\n    - \"Proper error handling\"\n    - \"No code duplication\"\n    - \"Proper logging\"\n\n  testing:\n    - \"Tests provided\"\n    - \"Test coverage >80%\"\n    - \"Edge cases handled\"\n    - \"All tests passing\"\n\n  documentation:\n    - \"Docstrings complete\"\n    - \"Type hints present\"\n    - \"README updated\"\n    - \"Examples provided\"\n\n  architecture:\n    - \"No tight coupling\"\n    - \"Components independent\"\n    - \"Scalable design\"\n    - \"Extensible for Phase 1.5\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Passes [category]\"\n  - \"⚠️  Warning: [issue]\"\n  - \"🛑 Blocker: [issue]\"\n  - \"📝 Recommendation: [suggestion]\"\n\n### ACTIVE SKILL: AUTOMATED TESTING GATE\n# Automated Testing Skill\nskill_id: \"automated-testing\"\nname: \"Automated Testing\"\ndescription: \"Capability to implement robust unit and integration tests and verify coverage gates\"\n\napplies_to:\n  - \"qa-engineer\"\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n\nchecklist:\n  unit_tests:\n    - \"Test files are located under tests/unit/ and start with test_\"\n    - \"Verify input and output tensor shapes on all key model layers\"\n    - \"Test mathematical stability (check that loss is positive, non-NaN, non-Inf)\"\n    - \"Test model reparameterization trick for correct stochastic behavior\"\n    - \"Test model checkpoint saving and loading metadata (epoch, loss, accuracy, config)\"\n    - \"Test reproducibility with fixed random seed constraints\"\n\n  integration_tests:\n    - \"Integration test files are located under tests/integration/\"\n    - \"Verify end-to-end model training runs and successfully reduces loss over epochs\"\n    - \"Verify early stopping triggers correctly when loss plateaus\"\n    - \"Verify data generation produces correct shape, bounds [0, 1], and correlations\"\n\n  coverage:\n    - \"Coverage configuration is maintained in .coveragerc\"\n    - \"pytest.ini defines term-missing and cov-fail-under=80\"\n    - \"Critical paths (model forward, loss calculation, training loop) target >90% coverage\"\n    - \"Ensure coverage stays above the 80.0% global gate\"\n\noutput_format:\n  - \"✅ Test Passed: [test name]\"\n  - \"❌ Test Failed: [issue details]\"\n  - \"📊 Coverage Status: [X]% (Target: >80%)\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEKLY-SYNC-CONTEXT)\n# Weekly Sync Context Handover\nhandover_id: \"weekly-sync\"\nname: \"Weekly Sync Context\"\ndescription: \"Passing context from one week to agents for next week\"\n\ntrigger: \"Friday end of week\"\n\ntemplate: |\n  Team sync context:\n\n  Week [N] Progress:\n  - ML Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - Backend Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - DevOps Lead: [What was accomplished]\n  - Architect: [Assessment of week]\n\n  Metrics:\n  - Model accuracy: [X]%\n  - API latency: [X]ms\n  - Test coverage: [X]%\n  - Infrastructure status: [Status]\n\n  Blockers:\n  - [Blocker 1]\n  - [Blocker 2]\n\n  Week [N+1] Focus:\n  - ML Engineer will: [Task]\n  - Backend Engineer will: [Task]\n  - DevOps Lead will: [Task]\n  - Architect will: [Task]\n\n  Questions for next week:\n  - [Question 1]\n  - [Question 2]\n\nagents_to_receive:\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\ntiming: \"Monday morning before work starts\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Create an abstract base class named DataSourceAdapter in src/vendors/base.py, defining methods for reading, normalizing, and validating data from various sources, and outline a per-vendor error handling strategy.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: src/vendors/base.py\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
