)`, then detail input/output contracts, and define common exceptions.\n\n\n**Defining Adapter's Scope**\n\nI'm now drafting the document content, starting with a title and status, the overview, and then diving into the details. I am carefully outlining the purpose of the Vendor Adapter layer. I'm focusing on providing a unified interface for data access. I'll make sure it abstracts complexities. I am aiming to ensure flexibility and extensibility by normalizing data formats into a canonical schema.\n\n```markdown\n# Vendor Adapter Design\n\n**Document Status :** DRAFT\n**Author:** Architect\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThe Vendor Adapter layer is a critical component of  the AI Agronomist platform, responsible for abstracting the complexities of data ingestion from various third-party greenhouse control systems and  sensors. Its primary purpose is to provide a unified interface for the rest of the application to access sensor data, regardless of the source  vendor, format, or protocol.\n\nThis decouples our core application logic from specific vendor implementations, allowing for greater flexibility and  extensibility. By normalizing disparate data formats into a single canonical schema, we ensure data consistency for downstream consumers like the LSTM \n```\n\n\n**Drafting Abstract Interface**\n\nI'm now drafting the content for the design document. I've begun defining the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface in Python, specifying the `__init__`, `connect`, and other methods. I'm focusing on clearly defining input parameters (like a configuration dictionary) and potential exceptions. I'll make sure to specify input and output data types, and any applicable data types or formats.\n\n\n**Defining Interface Methods**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface definition within the design document. I'm adding `connect()`, `read_data()`, and `disconnect()` methods with detailed descriptions and type hints. I'm also including `get_status()`, defining the expected return format for status information, and outlining potential exceptions like `ConnectionError` and `DataReadError`.\n\nI'm now drafting the design document, defining the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface in Python, specifying the `__init__`, `connect`, and other methods. I'm focusing on clearly defining input parameters (like a configuration dictionary) and potential exceptions. I'll make sure to specify input and output data types, and any applicable data types or formats.\n\n\n**Refining Method Specifications**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the specifications for the methods defined within the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface. I'm expanding the descriptions for each method, `connect()`, `read_data()`, and `disconnect()`, providing more context on their expected behaviors. I'm also ensuring that exception handling is clearly defined, and that the data types for input and output are correctly specified, including handling of timestamps. I'm also updating the status methods.\n\n\n","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"**Refining Method Specifications**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the specifications for the methods defined within the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface. I'm expanding the descriptions for each method, `connect()`, `read_data()`, and `disconnect()`, providing more context on their expected behaviors. I'm also ensuring that exception handling is clearly defined, and that the data types for input and output are correctly specified, including handling of timestamps. I'm also updating the status methods.\n\n\n","text":""}}
