2026-06-08 18:32:21,179 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"8","timestampMicros":"1780939941178766","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"47a103a70aad60504bd6cef88a0452bc","trajectoryId":"47a103a70aad60504bd6cef88a0452bc","stepIndex":1,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_USER","thinking":"**Defining the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I'm diving into the architecture design. My focus right now is on the overall structure, specifically for the REST API, Streamlit dashboard, and vendor adapter. I'm aiming for a single, comprehensive document at `docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md` to cover all three. I'm outlining their individual requirements.\n\n\n**Outlining the Requirements**\n\nI've got the initial requirements defined and I'm ready to document them. Specifically, I have outlined the endpoints, request/response schemas, and error handling for the REST API. I'm also planning the rate-limiting strategy. For the Streamlit dashboard, I've planned the various pages, state management, real-time refresh, and multi-tenant UI elements. I've also scoped the user threshold adjustment flow. Finally, I've outlined the database schema and indexes.\n\n\n**Structuring the Design**\n\nNow I'm creating the core file, `docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md`, to contain all architecture details. I'll structure it clearly with H1 titles and subsequent H2 and H3 headings for the API, dashboard, database, and vendor adapter components. For the REST API, I'm documenting endpoints (`/health`, `/api/upload`, `/api/inference`), schemas, error handling, and a rate-limiting strategy. I'm detailing dashboard pages (`sensor_data`, `anomalies`, etc.) and the chosen state management approach, real-time refresh, multi-tenant UI elements, and the threshold adjustment flow. The database section will specify the `SensorReading` table and necessary indexes. I will also propose a simple design for a vendor adapter.\n\n\n**Creating the File**\n\nI've begun crafting the `docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md` file. I'm focusing on structuring it with clear headings and markdown for readability. The initial sections will outline the REST API endpoints, schemas, and error handling, followed by Streamlit dashboard pages and state management, then database schema, and finally the vendor adapter, which I'll propose a simple design for as a starting point.\n\n\n","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"I will now design the REST API, Streamlit dashboard, and vendor adapter architecture, and document it in `docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md`."},"usageMetadata":{"promptTokenCount":"17599","cachedContentTokenCount":"0","candidatesTokenCount":"1619","thoughtsTokenCount":"599","totalTokenCount":"19817"}}
