 expected return format for status information, and outlining potential exceptions like `ConnectionError` and `DataReadError`.\n\nI'm now drafting the design document, defining the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface in Python, specifying the `__init__`, `connect`, and other methods. I'm focusing on clearly defining input parameters (like a configuration dictionary) and potential exceptions. I'll make sure to specify input and output data types, and any applicable data types or formats.\n\n\n**Refining Method Specifications**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the specifications for the methods defined within the `AbstractVendorAdapter` interface. I'm expanding the descriptions for each method, `connect()`, `read_data()`, and `disconnect()`, providing more context on their expected behaviors. I'm also ensuring that exception handling is clearly defined, and that the data types for input and output are correctly specified, including handling of timestamps. I'm also updating the status methods.\n\n\n**Refining Abstract Interface**\n\nI'm now revising the design document with a complete `AbstractVendorAdapter` definition, including method signatures and detailed descriptions. I've clearly defined expected input and output data types, along with common exceptions, and I'm ensuring comprehensive coverage. I'm focusing on ensuring it's a solid, functional and extensible foundation.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Defining CSV Adapter**\n\nI'm now starting to outline the `CSVAdapter` implementation within the design document. I'm detailing its configuration parameters (file path, column mapping), including error handling for file operations. I'm also describing the logic for how it reads data using Pandas. Finally, I'm documenting the normalization process to the canonical format.\n\n\n**Drafting CSV Implementation**\n\nI'm now detailing the implementation specifics of the `CSVAdapter`. I'm outlining how it will use the `pandas` library to read CSV data and the error-handling strategies for file operations and data parsing. I'm also describing the data normalization to map vendor-specific column names to the canonical format and providing examples.\n\n\n**Refining CSV Adapter**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the CSV adapter section. I'm adding more specific details. I'm clarifying how configuration parameters, like the file path and delimiter, are used. I am going into more detail about how it reads the data using pandas and the methods I've used. I'm also describing the error handling for missing files and parsing errors.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Defining Priva Adapter**\n\nI am now detailing the Priva Adapter (stub) section, focusing on providing essential configuration parameters like the API endpoint and API key. I am outlining the implementation notes, outlining connection testing with API calls and HTTP get requests for data. I am also planning error handling for API failures.\n\n\n**Refining Vendor Interface**\n\nI'm now revising the design document, making sure the overview aligns with the scope. I am including a clear definition of the vendor adapter's primary role. I am focused on the AbstractVendorAdapter interface, making sure it provides abstraction for diverse data sources and defining the role of the data normalization layer.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Defining CSV Implementation**\n\nI'm now detailing the content for the CSV Adapter, focusing on configuration and implementation notes. I am documenting the methods. I am defining how to read from a CSV file. I am also planning error-handling for missing files and parsing.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Defining Priva Adapter**\n\nI'm now outlining the Priva Adapter section, which is a stub for future work. I am focusing on the configuration parameters, such as API endpoint and key. I am outlining API calls and the error handling required.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Completing Adapter Design**\n\nI am now focusing on completing the draft. I am defining a roadmap for future extensibility and outlining all the sections of the design document. I am outlining how to add new adapters. I'm adding an Architectural Decision Record summary.\n\n\n**Defining Priva Adapter**\n\nI'm now detailing the Priva adapter's implementation outline, including API integration. I'm focusing on API calls with parameters. I'll cover the connection, data retrieval, error handling, and a future roadmap.\n\n\n","textDelta":"Okay, I will now create the `docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md` design document. I'll start by ensuring the directory exists and then write the content.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Okay, I will now create the `docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md` design document. I'll start by ensuring the directory exists and then write the content."}}
