2026-06-08 18:36:02,663 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780940162662832","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"37647c60363334d22658ef0ee6f7473f","trajectoryId":"37647c60363334d22658ef0ee6f7473f","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"Here is the current memory:\n\n# Agent Memory & Context\n\n## Project: AI Agronomist (Greenhouse Anomaly Detection)\n**Current Phase**: Phase 2 — API & DB Foundation\n\n## Completed Tasks (Week 1 & Week 2 Foundation)\n- ✅ **LSTM-VAE Architecture** (`src/models/lstm_vae.py`): Implemented with 2 LSTM layers in encoder/decoder and 8-dim latent space. Model includes type hints and docstrings.\n- ✅ **Synthetic Data Generator** (`src/models/data_generator.py`): Implemented basic realistic normal greenhouse sensor data with day/night cycles.\n- ✅ **Data Utilities** (`src/models/data_utils.py`): Data loading, preprocessing, dataloader creation, and denormalization.\n- ✅ **Configuration** (`src/config.py`): Hyperparameters for the model, training, and data generation.\n- ✅ **Training Pipeline** (`src/models/training.py`, `scripts/train_lstm_vae.py`): Training loops with early stopping, validation metrics, checkpointing, and tensorboard logging fully operational.\n- ✅ **API Boilerplate Structure** (`src/api/main.py`): Implemented initial REST API foundation, including FastAPI instantiation, CORS (access for Streamlit), exception handler filters (422, 404, 500), request ID middleware configuration, and health monitoring diagnostics interfaces.\n- ✅ **Database Session Router** (`src/db/session.py`): Configured SQLite asynchronous backend with SQLAlchemy 2.x async, get_db session dependency injection helper, and init_db startup hook.\n- ✅ **API & Boilerplate Unit Tests** (`tests/api/test_main.py`): Implemented thorough unit tests covering CORS, health checks, exception formatting, and mocked db failures.\n- ✅ **Unit Testing & Validation** (`tests/`): Pytest suite includes tests for mathematical stability, physical data constraints, and tensor shaping across batches.\n- ✅ **Architecture README**: Located in `src/models/README.md`.\n- ✅ **ADR-001**: LSTM-VAE Architecture ADR at `docs/architecture/ADR-001-lstm-vae-architecture.md`.\n- ✅ **ADR-002**: Synthetic Data Generation ADR at `docs/team/ADRs/ADR-002-synthetic-data-generation.md`.\n- ✅ **ADR-003**: Modular Architecture for Easy Phase 1.5 Scaling ADR at `docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-phase-1-5-architecture.md`.\n- ✅ **Architecture Assessment**: Completed a full architecture assessment, documented in `docs/team/ADRs/ARCHITECTURE_ASSESSMENT.md`.\n- ✅ **Database Models** (`src/db/models.py`, `src/db/__init__.py`, `tests/unit/test_db_models.py`): Designed isomorphically standard SQLAlchemy 2.x declarative schemas and a reusable `Base` class mapping. Established validation tests on in-memory SQLite backend demonstrating proper indexing for `tenant_id` and `timestamp`, timezone support, structural safety, nullable fields, and default column values.\n- ✅ **Alembic Database Migrations Suite** (`alembic.ini`, `src/db/migrations/env.py`, `src/db/migrations/script.py.mako`): Configured the entire migration facility leveraging local SQLAlchemy models. Integrated offline/online run configuration, dynamic environment variables connection overrides, and critical SQLite support with `render_as_batch=True`.\n\n## Pending / Next Steps\n- ⬜ **FastAPI Schema Validation** (`src/api/schemas/sensor_data.py`): Pydantic validation payload schemas.\n- ⬜ **Local Dev Environment / Dockerization**: Configure devops docker-compose development context.\n## Technical Notes\n- **Framework**: PyTorch, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.x Async.\n- **Database**: SQLite + aiosqlite as modern development proxy engine.\n- **Data Shapes**: `(batch_size, seq_len=20, input_dim=4)`.\n- **Sensors**: Temperature, Humidity, CO2, Light.\n\n\nHere is the new execution result:\n\nTask: Build Week 2 Phase 1 - Design and infrastructure setup for REST API, dashboard, and vendor abstraction.\n\nPhase 1 (parallel):\n\n- architect: Design REST API, Streamlit dashboard, and vendor adapter architecture.\n  Output: docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md, docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md\n  \n  Produce two design documents:\n  \n  1. docs/architecture/api_dashboard_design.md\n     Content:\n     - REST API endpoint specifications\n       * GET /health (simple health check)\n       * GET /health/db (database connectivity check)\n       * POST /api/upload (CSV file upload)\n       * POST /api/inference (model inference on sequences)\n     - Request/response schemas for each endpoint\n     - Error handling strategy (validation errors, server errors, etc.)\n     - Rate limiting strategy (prepare for Phase 1.5 multi-customer)\n     \n     - Streamlit Dashboard page specifications\n       * Pages: sensor_data.py, anomalies.py, thresholds.py, metrics.py\n       * State management (session state, caching)\n       * Real-time refresh strategy\n       * Multi-tenant filtering UI\n       * Threshold adjustment flow (how user changes threshold, saves to DB)\n     \n     - Database schema (high-level)\n       * SensorReading table structure\n       * Indexes needed\n       * Multi-tenant support (tenant_id)\n  \n  2. docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md\n     Content:\n     - Abstract vendor interface specification\n       * What methods must each adapter implement?\n       * Input/output contracts\n       * Error handling per vendor\n     - CSV adapter (current implementation)\n     - Priva adapter (stub for Phase 1.5)\n     - Data normalization layer (how different vendors' data gets standardized)\n     - Future extensibility (what other vendors might integrate?)\n\n- backend-engineer: Implement FastAPI application, SQLAlchemy models, Pydantic schemas, and Alembic setup.\n  Output: src/api/main.py, src/db/models.py, src/api/schemas/sensor_data.py, src/db/migrations/env.py\n  \n  Deliverables:\n  \n  1. src/api/main.py\n     - FastAPI() app instantiation\n     - CORS middleware (allow localhost:3000, :8501 for Streamlit)\n     - Dependency injection for database session\n     - Global exception handlers (422, 404, 500)\n     - Startup hook: initialize database (create tables if not exist)\n     - Shutdown hook: cleanup resources\n     - Request ID middleware (for logging)\n  \n  2. src/db/models.py\n     - SQLAlchemy ORM class: SensorReading\n       * id (primary key, int)\n       * tenant_id (str, indexed) - for multi-tenancy\n       * greenhouse_id (str)\n       * timestamp (datetime, indexed)\n       * temperature (float)\n       * humidity (float)\n       * co2 (float)\n       * light (float)\n       * anomaly_score (Optional[float])\n       * created_at (datetime, default=now)\n     - Base class for all models\n     - Table creation via SQLAlchemy declarative\n  \n  3. src/api/schemas/sensor_data.py\n     - Pydantic v2 models:\n       * SensorReadingCreate (for POST requests)\n       * SensorReadingResponse (for GET responses)\n       * UploadRequest (CSV file metadata)\n       * UploadResponse (upload result summary)\n       * InferenceRequest (sequence data for prediction)\n       * InferenceResponse (anomaly scores + metadata)\n     - All models must have type hints and docstrings\n  \n  4. src/db/migrations/ (Alembic setup)\n     - Initialize: alembic init\n     - Configure env.py to use SQLAlchemy models\n     - Setup for auto-generating migrations from models\n\n- ml-engineer: Implement improved inference engine and vendor adapter base class.\n  Output: src/models/inference.py (updated), src/vendors/base.py, src/vendors/csv_adapter.py\n  \n  Deliverables:\n  \n  1. src/models/inference.py (enhanced from Week 1)\n     - class AnomalyDetector:\n       * __init__(checkpoint_path: str, device: str = 'cpu')\n       * load_checkpoint() - load trained LSTM-VAE model\n       * predict(sequences: torch.Tensor) -> np.ndarray\n         - Input: (batch, seq_len, input_dim) tensor\n         - Output: (batch,) anomaly scores [0, 1]\n       * predict_batch(sequences: List[np.ndarray]) -> np.ndarray\n         - Handle variable-length batches\n       * get_reconstruction_error(x, x_recon) -> float\n       * cache_model_in_memory() - keep loaded model across requests\n     - Error handling:\n       * Model not found → clear error message\n       * Invalid input shapes → reshape or fail gracefully\n       * NaN/Inf in output → return error\n  \n  2. src/vendors/base.py\n     - Abstract base class: DataSourceAdapter\n       * async def read_data(source: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> np.ndarray\n         - Returns: (num_sequences, seq_len, input_dim)\n       * async def normalize_data(data: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray\n         - Standardize to [0, 1] range\n       * async def validate_data(data: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[bool, str]\n         - Check for NaN, Inf, out-of-range values\n       * Error handling strategy per vendor\n  \n  3. src/vendors/csv_adapter.py\n     - class CSVAdapter(DataSourceAdapter):\n       * __init__() - no special config for CSV\n       * read_data(file: UploadFile) -> np.ndarray\n         - Parse CSV (columns: timestamp, temp, humidity, co2, light)\n         - Return shape (N, 20, 4) sequences\n       * validate_data() - check for required columns, data types\n       * Normalize using config ranges\n\n- devops-lead: Setup structured logging and monitoring infrastructure.\n  Output: src/logging/config.py, src/api/middleware/logging.py, pyproject.toml (updated)\n  \n  Deliverables:\n  \n  1. src/logging/config.py\n     - Logging configuration (using structlog or logging)\n     - Output format: JSON (not pretty-printed)\n     - Log levels: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR\n     - Log file rotation (daily, max 10 files)\n     - Sensitive field redaction (hide API keys, tokens)\n     - Example log entry:\n       {\n         \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-08T10:30:00Z\",\n         \"level\": \"INFO\",\n         \"logger\": \"api.routes.inference\",\n         \"message\": \"inference completed\",\n         \"request_id\": \"abc-123\",\n         \"duration_ms\": 45,\n         \"model\": \"lstm_vae_v1\",\n         \"batch_size\": 32,\n         \"anomaly_detected\": true\n       }\n  \n  2. src/api/middleware/logging.py\n     - FastAPI middleware for request/response logging\n     - Capture:\n       * Request: method, path, headers (without secrets)\n       * Response: status code, duration, size\n       * Request ID (propagate through logs)\n     - Don't log request body (can be large)\n  \n  3. Metrics collection in inference:\n     - Inference latency (milliseconds)\n     - Batch size processed\n     - Model throughput (sequences/sec)\n     - Error count (failed inferences)\n     - These metrics exported to logs as JSON\n  \n  4. pyproject.toml (or requirements.txt)\n     - Add: structlog (or logging library of choice)\n     - Add: python-json-logger\n     - Ensure all dependencies pinned\n\nauto-proceed\nBuilt files:\n- [x] docs/architecture/vendor_adapter_design.md\n- [x] src/db/migrations/env.py\n- [x] src/vendors/csv_adapter.py\n- [x] pyproject.toml\nFailed files:\n\n\nReturn the updated AGENT_MEMORY.md file content.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Here is the current memory:\n\n# Agent Memory & Context\n\n## Project: AI Agronomist (Greenhouse Anomaly Detection)\n**Current Phase**: Phase 2 — API & DB Foundation\n\n## Completed Tasks (Week 1 & Week 2 Foundation)\n- ✅ **LSTM-VAE Architecture** (`src/models/lstm_vae.py`): Implemented with 2 LSTM layers in encoder/decoder and 8-dim latent space. Model includes type hints and docstrings.\n- ✅ **Synthetic Data Generator** (`src/models/data_generator.py`): Implemented basic realistic normal greenhouse sensor data with day/night cycles.\n- ✅ **Data Utilities** (`src/models/data_utils.py`): Data loading, preprocessing, dataloader creation, and denormalization.\n- ✅ **Configuration** (`src/config.py`): Hyperparameters for the model,