on. \\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1. Validating the input, including the shape of the sequences and the presence of `tenant_id`.\\n2. Loading the trained `LSTM-VAE` model.\\n3. Predicting anomaly scores for each sequence.\\n4. Saving the anomaly scores to the `SensorReading` table.\\n5. Returning a JSON response with the processing results, including any detected anomalies.\\n6. Implementing robust error handling for input errors and model loading failures.\\n7. Ensuring all functions have type hints and docstrings.\\n8. Implementing database transactions with rollbacks on error.\\n9. Using the application's configuration for any hardcoded paths or values.\\n10. Adding logging for all significant events, including info, warnings, and errors.\\n11. The output of this task is the new file: `src/api/routes/inference.py`\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/api/routes/health.py\",\"task\":\"Implement the health check endpoints.\\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1.  **`GET /health`**: This endpoint should return a JSON response with `{\\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\"}` and a `200` status code.\\n2.  **`GET /health/db`**: This endpoint should check the database connection by executing a simple query (`SELECT 1 FROM sensor_reading LIMIT 1`).\\n    *   On success, it should return `{\\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\", \\\"database\\\": \\\"connected\\\"}` with a `200` status code.\\n    *   On failure, it should return `{\\\"status\\\": \\\"error\\\", \\\"database\\\": \\\"disconnected\\\"}` with a `503` status code.\\n3. Ensuring all functions have type hints and docstrings.\\n4. Implementing error handling for the database connection check.\\n5. Using the application's configuration for any hardcoded paths or values.\\n6. Adding logging for all significant events, including info, warnings, and errors.\\n7. The output of this task is the new file: `src/api/routes/health.py`\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/db/seeds.py\",\"task\":\"Implement a test data seeding script.\\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1.  Create a function `seed_test_data(session, num_samples=100)` that creates sample `SensorReading` entries for testing purposes.\\n2.  The function should generate:\\n    *   100 normal sequences (anomaly\\\\_score \\u003c 0.3).\\n    *   10 high-anomaly sequences (anomaly\\\\_score \\u003e 0.8).\\n    *   Data for multiple tenants (`tenant_1`, `tenant_2`, `tenant_3`).\\n    *   Data for multiple greenhouses per tenant.\\n3.  Ensuring all functions have type hints and docstrings.\\n4.  The output of this task is the new file: `src/db/seeds.py`\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"alembic/versions/001_initial.py\",\"task\":\"Create the initial Alembic migration.\\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1.  Use `alembic revision --autogenerate -m \\\"Initial schema\\\"` to create the initial migration.\\n2.  The migration should create the `sensor_reading` table with appropriate columns and constraints.\\n3.  The migration should set up indexes on (`tenant_id`, `timestamp`).\\n4.  The migration should add `NOT NULL` constraints on required fields.\\n5.  Verify the migration by running `alembic upgrade head` and ensuring the table is created correctly.\\n6.  The output of this task is the new migration file: `alembic/versions/001_initial.py`\"},{\"agent\":\"backend-engineer\",\"output_file\":\"src/api/main.py\",\"task\":\"Update the main FastAPI application file `src/api/main.py`.\\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1.  Add the necessary imports for the new routes: `health`, `upload`, and `inference`.\\n2.  Register the new routes with the FastAPI application instance.\\n3.  Add a startup event hook (`@app.on_event(\\\"startup\\\")`) to run `alembic upgrade head` automatically when the application starts.\\n4.  Ensuring that the changes are correctly integrated with the existing application structure.\\n5.  The output of this task is the updated file: `src/api/main.py`\"}],\"phase\":1},{\"agents\":[{\"agent\":\"code-reviewer\",\"context_from\":[\"backend-engineer\"],\"output_file\":\"src/api/routes/upload.py,src/api/routes/inference.py,src/api/routes/health.py,src/db/seeds.py,alembic/versions/001_initial.py,src/api/main.py\",\"task\":\"Review all the files generated by the `backend-engineer`. \\nYou are responsible for the following:\\n1.  Check for correctness, performance, security, and style.\\n2.  Verify that all requirements from the task description have been met.\\n3.  Ensure that the code is well-documented with type hints and docstrings.\\n4.  Check for proper error handling and database transaction management.\\n5.  Verify that no hardcoded paths or values are used.\\n6.  Ensure that logging is implemented correctly.\\n7.  If any issues are found, you can directly edit the files to fix them.\\n8.  The output of this task are the reviewed and potentially corrected files.\"}],\"phase\":2}]}"}}}
