2026-06-08 18:46:21,778 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780940781777925","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","trajectoryId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== backend-engineer output ===\n\"\"\"\nMain FastAPI application entry point for the AI Agronomist platform.\n\nThis module instantiates the FastAPI app, configures CORS middleware for localhost\nStreamlit access, registers global error handlers, setups dependency injection for db sessions,\nconfigures lifecycle startup/shutdown hooks (database table creation and engine disposal), and\nwires up custom Request ID middleware for end-to-end logging traceability.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom typing import AsyncGenerator, Callable\n\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Request, Response, status\nfrom fastapi.exceptions import RequestValidationError\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom starlette.exceptions import HTTPException as StarletteHTTPException\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy import text\n\n# Try to load formatted logging configurations from our devops setup\ntry:\n    from src.logging.config import setup_logging\n    setup_logging()\nexcept ImportError:\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\nfrom src.db.session import engine, get_db, init_db\nfrom src.api.routes import health\n\n# Initialize module logger\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"api.main\")\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI) -> AsyncGenerator[None, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Asynchronous lifespan manager handling startup database initialization\n    and shutdown resource cleanup.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting up FastAPI application...\")\n    try:\n        # Initialize database tables on startup\n        await init_db()\n        logger.info(\"Database schema initialized successfully.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.critical(f\"Failed to initialize database: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n        raise e\n\n    yield\n\n    logger.info(\"Shutting down FastAPI application...\")\n    try:\n        # Dispose of SQLAlchemy pool and close active connections\n        await engine.dispose()\n        logger.info(\"Database connection engine successfully disposed.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f\"Failed to cleanly dispose of database resources: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n\n\n# Instantiate the FastAPI app\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"AI Agronomist API\",\n    description=\"REST API for multi-tenant greenhouse telemetry data ingestion, inference, and threshold management.\",\n    version=\"1.0.0\",\n    lifespan=lifespan,\n)\n\n# CORS configurations allowing Streamlit dashboard and local React/Vue dev tools\norigins = [\n    \"http://localhost\",\n    \"http://localhost:3000\",   # Default React developer port\n    \"http://localhost:8501\",   # Default Streamlit dashboard port\n    \"http://127.0.0.1\",\n    \"http://127.0.0.1:3000\",\n    \"http://127.0.0.1:8501\",\n]\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=origins,\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\n\n@app.middleware(\"http\")\nasync def add_request_id_and_log_middleware(request: Request, call_next: Callable) -> Response:\n    \"\"\"\n    Middleware that generates and injects an X-Request-ID for all requests,\n    logs incoming and outgoing paths with duration tracking, and injects\n    request context parameters into the response headers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Extract existing Request ID from client header, or generate a fresh UUID4\n    request_id = request.headers.get(\"X-Request-ID\") or str(uuid.uuid4())\n    request.state.request_id = request_id\n\n    # Benchmarking request start\n    start_time = time.time()\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Request started: {request.method} {request.url.path} | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n\n    try:\n        response = await call_next(request)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Just in case an unhandled exception manages to escape call_next\n        process_time_ms = (time.time() - start_time) * 1000.0\n        logger.error(\n            f\"Exception escaped middleware: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n            f\"Duration: {process_time_ms:.2f}ms | RequestID: {request_id} | Error: {e}\",\n            exc_info=True\n        )\n        raise e\n\n    # Benchmarking request completion\n    duration_ms = (time.time() - start_time) * 1000.0\n\n    # Inject tracking ID and diagnostic header into client response\n    response.headers[\"X-Request-ID\"] = request_id\n    response.headers[\"X-Process-Time-Ms\"] = f\"{duration_ms:.2f}\"\n\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Request completed: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"Status: {response.status_code} | Duration: {duration_ms:.2f}ms | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n\n    return response\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# Global Exception Handlers\n# =============================================================================\n\n@app.exception_handler(RequestValidationError)\nasync def validation_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: RequestValidationError) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catches 422 Unprocessable Entity validation errors (such as Pydantic structural errors).\n    Restructures the output with clear validation feedback and correlates with Request ID.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    errors = exc.errors()\n    logger.warning(\n        f\"Validation failure: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"RequestID: {request_id} | Validation errors: {errors}\"\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n        content={\n            \"detail\": errors,\n            \"message\": \"The incoming payload validation failed. Please check the structure of your fields.\",\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n@app.exception_handler(StarletteHTTPException)\nasync def http_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: StarletteHTTPException) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catches standard Starlette / FastAPI HTTPException.\n    Simplifies the error structure and stamps details with Request ID.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    logger.warning(\n        f\"HTTP operational error: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"Status: {exc.status_code} | Reason: {exc.detail} | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=exc.status_code,\n        content={\n            \"message\": exc.detail,\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n@app.exception_handler(Exception)\nasync def default_unhandled_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: Exception) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catch-all global exception handler returning a sanitized 500 error payload to\n    the client while fully logging the internal traceback for backend engineering auditing.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    logger.error(\n        f\"Unhandled application exception: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"RequestID: {request_id} | Error: {str(exc)}\",\n        exc_info=True,\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n        content={\n            \"message\": \"An internal server error occurred. Please contact system administrators.\",\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# Health & Status Diagnostics Routes\n# =============================================================================\n\napp.include_router(health.router)\n\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review all the files generated by the `backend-engineer`. \nYou are responsible for the following:\n1.  Check for correctness, performance, security, and style.\n2.  Verify that all requirements from the task description have been met.\n3.  Ensure that the code is well-documented with type hints and docstrings.\n4.  Check for proper error handling and database transaction management.\n5.  Verify that no hardcoded paths or values are used.\n6.  Ensure that logging is implemented correctly.\n7.  If any issues are found, you can directly edit the files to fix them.\n8.  The output of this task are the reviewed and potentially corrected files.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: src/api/routes/upload.py,src/api/routes/inference.py,src/api/routes/health.py,src/db/seeds.py,alembic/versions/001_initial.py,src/api/main.py\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== backend-engineer output ===\n\"\"\"\nMain FastAPI application entry point for the AI Agronomist platform.\n\nThis module instantiates the FastAPI app, configures CORS middleware for localhost\nStreamlit access, registers global error handlers, setups dependency injection for db sessions,\nconfigures lifecycle startup/shutdown hooks (database table creation and engine disposal), and\nwires up custom Request ID middleware for end-to-end logging traceability.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\nfrom typing import AsyncGenerator, Callable\n\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, Request, Response, status\nfrom fastapi.exceptions import RequestValidationError\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom starlette.exceptions import HTTPException as StarletteHTTPException\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy import text\n\n# Try to load formatted logging configurations from our devops setup\ntry:\n    from src.logging.config import setup_logging\n    setup_logging()\nexcept ImportError:\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n\nfrom src.db.session import engine, get_db, init_db\nfrom src.api.routes import health\n\n# Initialize module logger\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"api.main\")\n\n\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI) -> AsyncGenerator[None, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Asynchronous lifespan manager handling startup database initialization\n    and shutdown resource cleanup.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting up FastAPI application...\")\n    try:\n        # Initialize database tables on startup\n        await init_db()\n        logger.info(\"Database schema initialized successfully.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.critical(f\"Failed to initialize database: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n        raise e\n\n    yield\n\n    logger.info(\"Shutting down FastAPI application...\")\n    try:\n        # Dispose of SQLAlchemy pool and close active connections\n        await engine.dispose()\n        logger.info(\"Database connection engine successfully disposed.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f\"Failed to cleanly dispose of database resources: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n\n\n# Instantiate the FastAPI app\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"AI Agronomist API\",\n    description=\"REST API for multi-tenant greenhouse telemetry data ingestion, inference, and threshold management.\",\n    version=\"1.0.0\",\n    lifespan=lifespan,\n)\n\n# CORS configurations allowing Streamlit dashboard and local React/Vue dev tools\norigins = [\n    \"http://localhost\",\n    \"http://localhost:3000\",   # Default React developer port\n    \"http://localhost:8501\",   # Default Streamlit dashboard port\n    \"http://127.0.0.1\",\n    \"http://127.0.0.1:3000\",\n    \"http://127.0.0.1:8501\",\n]\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=origins,\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\n\n@app.middleware(\"http\")\nasync def add_request_id_and_log_middleware(request: Request, call_next: Callable) -> Response:\n    \"\"\"\n    Middleware that generates and injects an X-Request-ID for all requests,\n    logs incoming and outgoing paths with duration tracking, and injects\n    request context parameters into the response headers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Extract existing Request ID from client header, or generate a fresh UUID4\n    request_id = request.headers.get(\"X-Request-ID\") or str(uuid.uuid4())\n    request.state.request_id = request_id\n\n    # Benchmarking request start\n    start_time = time.time()\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Request started: {request.method} {request.url.path} | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n\n    try:\n        response = await call_next(request)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Just in case an unhandled exception manages to escape call_next\n        process_time_ms = (time.time() - start_time) * 1000.0\n        logger.error(\n            f\"Exception escaped middleware: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n            f\"Duration: {process_time_ms:.2f}ms | RequestID: {request_id} | Error: {e}\",\n            exc_info=True\n        )\n        raise e\n\n    # Benchmarking request completion\n    duration_ms = (time.time() - start_time) * 1000.0\n\n    # Inject tracking ID and diagnostic header into client response\n    response.headers[\"X-Request-ID\"] = request_id\n    response.headers[\"X-Process-Time-Ms\"] = f\"{duration_ms:.2f}\"\n\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Request completed: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"Status: {response.status_code} | Duration: {duration_ms:.2f}ms | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n\n    return response\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# Global Exception Handlers\n# =============================================================================\n\n@app.exception_handler(RequestValidationError)\nasync def validation_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: RequestValidationError) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catches 422 Unprocessable Entity validation errors (such as Pydantic structural errors).\n    Restructures the output with clear validation feedback and correlates with Request ID.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    errors = exc.errors()\n    logger.warning(\n        f\"Validation failure: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"RequestID: {request_id} | Validation errors: {errors}\"\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,\n        content={\n            \"detail\": errors,\n            \"message\": \"The incoming payload validation failed. Please check the structure of your fields.\",\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n@app.exception_handler(StarletteHTTPException)\nasync def http_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: StarletteHTTPException) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catches standard Starlette / FastAPI HTTPException.\n    Simplifies the error structure and stamps details with Request ID.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    logger.warning(\n        f\"HTTP operational error: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"Status: {exc.status_code} | Reason: {exc.detail} | RequestID: {request_id}\"\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=exc.status_code,\n        content={\n            \"message\": exc.detail,\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n@app.exception_handler(Exception)\nasync def default_unhandled_exception_handler(request: Request, exc: Exception) -> JSONResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Catch-all global exception handler returning a sanitized 500 error payload to\n    the client while fully logging the internal traceback for backend engineering auditing.\n    \"\"\"\n    request_id = getattr(request.state, \"request_id\", \"unknown\")\n    logger.error(\n        f\"Unhandled application exception: {request.method} {request.url.path} | \"\n        f\"RequestID: {request_id} | Error: {str(exc)}\",\n        exc_info=True,\n    )\n    return JSONResponse(\n        status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n        content={\n            \"message\": \"An internal server error occurred. Please contact system administrators.\",\n            \"request_id\": request_id,\n        },\n    )\n\n\n# =============================================================================\n# Health & Status Diagnostics Routes\n# =============================================================================\n\napp.include_router(health.router)\n\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review all the files generated by the `backend-engineer`. \nYou are responsible for the following:\n1.  Check for correctness, performance, security, and style.\n2.  Verify that all requirements from the task description have been met.\n3.  Ensure that the code is well-documented with type hints and docstrings.\n4.  Check for proper error handling and database transaction management.\n5.  Verify that no hardcoded paths or values are used.\n6.  Ensure that logging is implemented correctly.\n7.  If any issues are found, you can directly edit the files to fix them.\n8.  The output of this task are the reviewed and potentially corrected files.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: src/api/routes/upload.py,src/api/routes/inference.py,src/api/routes/health.py,src/db/seeds.py,alembic/versions/001_initial.py,src/api/main.py\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
