2026-06-08 18:46:46,127 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"18","timestampMicros":"1780940806127066","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","trajectoryId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","stepIndex":4,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"ADR-001 creation","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-001-architecture.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":0,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-001: Monolithic vs. Microservices Architecture","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Status**: Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Date**: 2026-06-08","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Author**: AI Architect","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"The AI Agronomist platform requires a robust, scalable, and maintainable architecture to support real-time data ingestion, model inference, and a user-facing dashboard. We need to decide between a monolithic architecture, where all components are tightly integrated into a single application, and a microservices architecture, where each component is an independent, deployable service.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"We will adopt a **modular monolithic architecture** for the initial development phase. This approach provides a balance between development speed and future scalability. We will separate concerns into distinct modules (e.g., `api`, `models`, `database`) within a single FastAPI application.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Rationale","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Development Speed**: A monolithic architecture is faster to develop and deploy initially, as it avoids the complexity of distributed systems.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Simplified Debugging**: Tracing requests and debugging issues is more straightforward in a single codebase.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Reduced Overhead**: We avoid the operational overhead of managing multiple services, container orchestration, and complex CI/CD pipelines.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Future-Proofing**: By designing the monolith with clear module boundaries, we can more easily extract services into a microservices architecture as the platform grows and traffic increases.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Scalability**: Scaling will be monolithic; we cannot scale individual components independently. This is an acceptable trade-off for the initial phase.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Technology Stack**: We are committed to a single technology stack (FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, etc.) for the entire application.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Deployment**: The entire application must be deployed for any change, which can slow down the deployment process as the application grows.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"}]}]}}}
