2026-06-08 18:46:57,778 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"29","timestampMicros":"1780940817777677","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","trajectoryId":"5f4da09698aa7935bcb388b10193ff5c","stepIndex":8,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"ADR-003 creation","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-architecture.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":0,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-003: Modular Monolith and Service Boundaries","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Status**: Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Date**: 2026-06-08","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Author**: AI Architect","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"To ensure the long-term maintainability and scalability of the AI Agronomist platform, we need to establish clear boundaries between different components of the system. This is crucial for a modular monolithic architecture, as it prevents tight coupling and facilitates future migration to microservices.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"We will structure the application into the following distinct modules:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **`src/api`**: Handles all API-related concerns, including routing, request/response models, and authentication.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **`src/models`**: Contains the machine learning models, including the LSTM-VAE, as well as data processing and feature engineering logic.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **`src/db`**: Manages all database interactions, including schema definitions, session management, and CRUD operations.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **`src/config`**: Centralizes all application configuration, such as database connection strings, model hyperparameters, and external API keys.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Rationale","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Separation of Concerns**: Each module has a single, well-defined responsibility, which makes the codebase easier to understand, maintain, and test.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Reduced Coupling**: The modules will communicate through well-defined interfaces, which reduces coupling and allows for independent development and testing.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Scalability**: The modular design makes it easier to identify performance bottlenecks and scale individual components as needed.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Future-Proofing**: The clear boundaries between modules will make it easier to extract services into a microservices architecture in the future.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Increased Complexity**: The modular design adds some complexity to the codebase, as it requires careful management of dependencies and interfaces between modules.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Potential for Circular Dependencies**: We must be vigilant to avoid circular dependencies between modules, which can lead to a tightly coupled and difficult-to-maintain codebase.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"}]}]}}}
