riting tests that verify correct initialization with no config, that connections and disconnections change the adapter's state, and that reading when disconnected raises an appropriate error. I want to test the `file_path`, `connected`, and `name` properties.\n\n\n**Testing Adapter Reading**\n\nI'm now writing tests for the CSV adapter's `read` functionality. I'm verifying the behavior when `read` is called without a file path in the config. I'm ensuring it generates mock telemetry data and that the resulting Pandas DataFrame has the expected columns and data types. I'm making sure it raises a specific error if `connect` is not called first. I'm also ensuring the successful behavior when the file is valid.\n\n\n**Implementing Read Tests**\n\nI'm now writing tests that verify the `read` method for several error conditions. I'm ensuring it produces the correct Pandas DataFrame with valid files, raises a `DataReadError` for non-existent and corrupt files, and also ensures that `read` handles Pandas parsing failures. I'm focusing on rigorous error handling.\n\n\n\n**Testing Normalization Function**\n\nI'm now testing the `normalize` function with the same CSVAdapter instance. I'm verifying the normalization of naive local datetime timestamps, ensuring they correctly localize to UTC. I've set up tests to assert that the resulting DataFrame has the expected columns and that the timestamp column is in UTC timezone. I'm also ensuring the values in the DataFrame are properly populated. Additionally, I'm verifying the data types are coerced to float64, and that the temperature column has the correct value.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Timezone Conversion**\n\nI'm now writing and testing `test_normalize_success_tz_aware`, which verifies correct UTC conversion with timezone offsets. I'm also ensuring the code works when columns are missing. I am validating that the resulting DataFrame has correct columns and data, with the timezone properly adjusted. I have verified the correct UTC conversion with assertions about the timestamp and its hour value.\n\n\n**Testing Error Handling**\n\nI'm now testing the error handling for various failure scenarios. I'm verifying that invalid timestamps and numeric data trigger `NormalizationError` exceptions as expected. I'm also preparing to test the case where required columns are missing, ensuring it raises the correct error. I am making sure the adapter functions robustly in the face of bad data.\n\n\n","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"**Testing Error Handling**\n\nI'm now testing the error handling for various failure scenarios. I'm verifying that invalid timestamps and numeric data trigger `NormalizationError` exceptions as expected. I'm also preparing to test the case where required columns are missing, ensuring it raises the correct error. I am making sure the adapter functions robustly in the face of bad data.\n\n\n","text":""}}
