rsion with assertions about the timestamp and its hour value.\n\n\n**Testing Error Handling**\n\nI'm now testing the error handling for various failure scenarios. I'm verifying that invalid timestamps and numeric data trigger `NormalizationError` exceptions as expected. I'm also preparing to test the case where required columns are missing, ensuring it raises the correct error. I am making sure the adapter functions robustly in the face of bad data.\n\n\n**Validating Out-of-Bounds Cases**\n\nI'm now focusing on validating the edge cases where the `validate` function should raise a `DataValidationError`. I'm verifying the behavior of the `validate` function with temperature readings outside the acceptable range, and ensuring the correct error message is raised. I'm also ensuring the test functions robustly with generic Python Exceptions.\n\n\n**Testing Data Validation**\n\nI'm now writing tests to validate the data validation flow. I'm focusing on ensuring exceptions are correctly raised when None is passed to the validation helper. I'm also preparing to test a robust multi-step `get_data` flow. I'm making sure it can handle both file paths and mock data. I'll verify the data returned by the adaptor has the expected shape and timezone.\n\n\n\n","textDelta":" fully aligns with the specified architecture and is designed to achieve near 100% statement and branch coverage of `src/vendors/csv_","thinkingDelta":"","text":"I will now create the file `tests/vendors/test_csv_adapter.py` and write the comprehensive test suite directly to it. This test suite fully aligns with the specified architecture and is designed to achieve near 100% statement and branch coverage of `src/vendors/csv_"}}
