2026-06-09 10:53:55,401 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780998835401524","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","trajectoryId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== backend-engineer output ===\n\"\"\"\nVendors subpackage containing adapters, abstract base classes, and exception hierarchies\nfor sensor telemetry ingestion.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .base import (\n    AbstractVendorAdapter,\n    DataReadError,\n    DataSourceAdapter,\n    DataSourceConnectionError,\n    DataValidationError,\n    NormalizationError,\n    VendorError,\n)\nfrom .csv_adapter import CSVAdapter\nfrom .priva_client import PrivaClient\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"DataSourceAdapter\",\n    \"AbstractVendorAdapter\",\n    \"CSVAdapter\",\n    \"PrivaClient\",\n    \"VendorError\",\n    \"DataSourceConnectionError\",\n    \"DataReadError\",\n    \"NormalizationError\",\n    \"DataValidationError\",\n]\n\n\n=== qa-engineer output ===\n\"\"\"Tests for vendor abstractions and adapters.\"\"\"\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review the implementation of the vendor abstraction layer, including the `DataSourceAdapter` interface, `CSVAdapter`, `PrivaClient` stub, and all the corresponding unit tests. Provide feedback on correctness, adherence to the requirements, and code quality in a markdown report.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: /Users/eugenesidorov/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d2121f0c96402a3ee69a61f1e3ce6be1/code_review_phase4.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that im