2026-06-09 10:55:40,851 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"151","timestampMicros":"1780998940850499","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","trajectoryId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","stepIndex":40,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Overwriting ADR-001","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-001-architecture.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":26,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-001: Monolithic vs. Microservices Architecture","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Status**: Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Date**: 2026-06-08","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Author**: AI Architect","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"# ADR-001: Vendor Abstraction Layer for Data Ingestion","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Date:** 2026-06-09","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Status:** Adopted","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"The AI Agronomist platform requires a robust, scalable, and maintainable architecture to support real-time data ingestion, model inference, and a user-facing dashboard. We need to decide between a monolithic architecture, where all components are tightly integrated into a single application, and a microservices architecture, where each component is an independent, deployable service.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"The AI Agronomist platform needs to ingest sensor data from a variety of sources, including CSV files, third-party APIs (e.g., Priva), and potentially other formats in the future. Each data source has its own unique API, data format, and error handling characteristics. To avoid tightly coupling the core application to the specifics of each data source, a flexible and extensible data ingestion framework is required.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"We will adopt a **modular monolithic architecture** for the initial development phase. This approach provides a balance between development speed and future scalability. We will separate concerns into distinct modules (e.g., `api`, `models`, `database`) within a single FastAPI application.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"## Rationale","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Development Speed**: A monolithic architecture is faster to develop and deploy initially, as it avoids the complexity of distributed systems.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Simplified Debugging**: Tracing requests and debugging issues is more straightforward in a single codebase.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Reduced Overhead**: We avoid the operational overhead of managing multiple services, container orchestration, and complex CI/CD pipelines.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Future-Proofing**: By designing the monolith with clear module boundaries, we can more easily extract services into a microservices architecture as the platform grows and traffic increases.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"We will implement a vendor abstraction layer that decouples the core application from the specifics of data ingestion. This layer will consist of the following components:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **`DataSourceAdapter`:** An abstract base class that defines a common interface for all vendor adapters. This interface will include methods for connecting to the data source, reading data, normalizing data to a canonical schema, and validating the data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Concrete Adapters:** A set of concrete classes that implement the `DataSourceAdapter` interface for specific data sources. For example, we will have a `CSVAdapter` for reading data from CSV files and a `PrivaClient` for interacting with the Priva API.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Canonical Data Schema:** A standardized data schema that all vendor adapters will be required to normalize their data to. This will ensure that all data ingested into the platform has a consistent format, regardless of its source.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Custom Exception Hierarchy:** A custom exception hierarchy that will be used to handle errors that occur during the data ingestion process. This will allow for more granular and informative error handling.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"- **Scalability**: Scaling will be monolithic; we cannot scale individual components independently. This is an acceptable trade-off for the initial phase.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Technology Stack**: We are committed to a single technology stack (FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, etc.) for the entire application.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Deployment**: The entire application must be deployed for any change, which can slow down the deployment process as the application grows.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"### Positive","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Loose Coupling:** The vendor abstraction layer will decouple the core application from the specifics of data ingestion, making the system more modular and easier to maintain.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Extensibility:** The use of a common interface will make it easy to add new data sources in the future by simply creating a new adapter.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Improved Testability:** The abstraction layer will make it easier to test the data ingestion process in isolation, without the need for real data sources.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Improved Error Handling:** The custom exception hierarchy will allow for more specific and informative error handling, which will make it easier to identify and troubleshoot issues.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### Negative","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Increased Complexity:** The introduction of an abstraction layer will add some complexity to the system. However, we believe that the benefits of loose coupling and extensibility far outweigh this drawback.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Potential for Performance Overhead:** There may be a small amount of performance overhead associated with the abstraction layer. However, we do not expect this to be significant, and we will monitor the performance of the system to ensure that it remains within acceptable limits.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"}]}]}}}
