2026-06-09 10:55:45,551 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"157","timestampMicros":"1780998945551344","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","trajectoryId":"893b23b93588852d98ef9195715e4552","stepIndex":42,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Overwriting ADR-002","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-002-synthetic-data.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":25,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-002: Synthetic Data Generation for Model Training","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Status**: Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Date**: 2026-06-08","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Author**: AI Architect","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"# ADR-002: Synthetic Data Generation for Testing and Development","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Date:** 2026-06-09","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Status:** Adopted","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"The LSTM-VAE model requires a large and diverse dataset for effective training. Real-world sensor data from greenhouses is often scarce, noisy, and may not cover all possible scenarios. To address this, we need a strategy for generating synthetic data that accurately reflects the characteristics of real data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"The AI Agronomist platform requires a reliable and consistent source of data for testing and development purposes. Real-world sensor data can be difficult to obtain, and it may not always be suitable for testing, as it may not contain the specific edge cases or error conditions that need to be tested.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"We will implement a **synthetic data generator** using statistical methods and domain-specific knowledge. The generator will create time-series data that mimics the patterns of temperature, humidity, and CO2 levels observed in a real greenhouse, including anomalies and sensor noise.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"## Rationale","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Data Availability**: Synthetic data generation allows us to create a large dataset for training and testing, reducing our reliance on limited real-world data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Controlled Scenarios**: We can generate data for specific scenarios, such as sensor failures or unusual environmental conditions, to improve the model's robustness.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Cost-Effective**: Generating data is significantly cheaper and faster than collecting and labeling real-world data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Iterative Model Improvement**: As we collect more real data, we can refine the synthetic data generator to produce more realistic data, creating a feedback loop for continuous model improvement.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"We will implement a synthetic data generator that can create realistic and representative sensor data for testing and development purposes. This generator will be able to produce data that conforms to the canonical data schema, and it will be configurable to allow for the generation of a wide range of scenarios, including both \"happy path\" and error conditions.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"- **Data Realism**: The synthetic data may not perfectly capture the complexity and nuances of real-world data, which could lead to a model that performs well on synthetic data but not on real data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Maintenance**: The synthetic data generator will require ongoing maintenance and refinement as we learn more about the data and the model's performance.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"### Positive","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Improved Testability:** The synthetic data generator will make it easier to test the data ingestion pipeline, as it will provide a reliable and consistent source of data.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Reduced Reliance on Real Data:** The use of synthetic data will reduce our reliance on real-world sensor data, which can be difficult and expensive to obtain.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Faster Development Cycles:** The ability to quickly and easily generate data for testing will help to speed up the development process.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Improved Code Quality:** The ability to test a wide range of scenarios will help to improve the quality of the code.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### Negative","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Increased Complexity:** The implementation of a synthetic data generator will add some complexity to the system.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"*   **Maintenance Overhead:** The synthetic data generator will need to be maintained and updated as the platform evolves.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"}]}]}}}
