2026-06-09 11:00:09,443 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1780999209442815","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"e64a7f8e0e97b27a7aa0744ee2b8c15e","trajectoryId":"e64a7f8e0e97b27a7aa0744ee2b8c15e","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"Here is the current memory:\n\n# Agent Memory\n\nThis document summarises the current stage, completed accomplishments, pending actions, and technical constraints of the Antigravity Agent (Code Reviewer & Quality Engineer).\n\n## Current Phase\nWe are currently executing **Week 2, Phase 4**: implementing and validating the Vendor Abstraction Layer, building the Priva API Client Stub, and delivering robust, comprehensive unit and end-to-end API test suites.\n\n## Completed Tasks\n*   **API Health Endpoint Test Overhaul ([tests/api/test_health.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_health.py))**:\n    *   Rewrote the broken health check tests to target 100% logic coverage of `/health` and `/health/db` routes in the API route definition.\n    *   Resolved severe integration/import bugs in the existing test layout: fixed the broken `from src.main import app` import to `from src.api.main import app`.\n    *   Corrected the invalid mock targets in database health-check testing: replaced `@patch('src.api.endpoints.health.get_db_session')` with FastAPI `dependency_overrides` on `get_db` to properly simulate real-world service injection.\n    *   Implemented exhaustive error path coverage: simulated standard successful connections, SQLite database locking failures (`SQLAlchemyError`), and general unhandled system exceptions (`Exception`).\n    *   Verified critical middleware functionality: validated CORS access control headers for stream applications, custom tracing correlation injection via `X-Request-ID` headers, and process timers.\n    *   Ensured authorization-free access validation on health endpoints.\n*   **Abstract Abstraction Design (`src/vendors/base.py`)**: Implemented the `DataSourceAdapter` interface mapping raw inputs to standard, multi-tenant schemas. Integrated custom hierarchical exceptions (`VendorError`, `DataSourceConnectionError`, `DataReadError`, `NormalizationError`, `DataValidationError`) and standard-validated columns.\n*   **CSV Adapter Implementation (`src/vendors/csv_adapter.py`)**: Formulated CSV-parsing mechanisms that ingest timezone-naive and timezone-aware timestamps, perform data range bound validations, and output pristine canonical columns.\n*   **Priva API Client Scaffold (`src/vendors/priva_client.py`)**: Engineered a concrete client stub enabling authentication hook scaffold (`_authenticate`), greenhouse polling (`_list_greenhouses`), and sensor reads (`_get_sensor_data`) with high-fidelity simulated response payloads matching our target sensor structure.\n*   **Comprehensive Testing Suite (`tests/vendors/`)**: Completed full test automation across happy/unhappy and boundary exception states:\n    *   [test_csv_adapter.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/vendors/test_csv_adapter.py) covers initialization, parsing of missing or invalid columns, non-numeric values, and empty structures.\n    *   [test_priva_stub.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/vendors/test_priva_stub.py) validates compliance to the interface, mock fetching, boundary validations, and method contracts.\n*   **Architecture & Quality Audit Documentation**:\n    *   Produced a code review report detailing structural and quality assessments for the source files.\n    *   Documented system architecture decisions in:\n        *   [ADR-001: Vendor Abstraction Layer](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-001-architecture.md)\n        *   [ADR-002: Synthetic Data Generation](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-002-synthetic-data.md)\n        *   [ADR-003: Modular Architecture](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-architecture.md)\n    *   Generated [week1-review.md](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/review/week1-review.md) summarizing foundational status.\n\n## Pending/Next Steps\n*   **Orchestration Support**: Integrate the newly minted `DataSourceAdapter` implementations directly with the main ingest pipeline and model training orchestration layers.\n*   **Dynamic Source Selection**: Allow quick switching between \"csv\" and \"priva\" ingestion based on tenant configuration settings without code modifications.\n*   **OAuth / Real Endpoint Upgrades (Phase 1.5)**: Replace mockup methods in `PrivaClient` with active network endpoints.\n*   **Run All Tests & Confirm Coverage**: Run coverage reports locally or in CI continuously to maintain >90% coverage goals constraints.\n\n## Technical Notes\n*   **Bugs Discovered & Reported**:\n    *   *Bug in existing `/health` test suite*: The legacy [tests/api/test_health.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_health.py) contained broken import references (`from src.main import app` instead of `from src.api.main import app`) and attempted to patch a non-existent module function `src.api.endpoints.health.get_db_session` instead of using FastAPI's standard dependency injection override mechanism, causing test discovery to fail. Overwritten with fully corrected and robust tests.\n*   **Canonical Sensor Schema**:\n    *   `timestamp`: timezone-aware datetime64 formatted in UTC\n    *   `temperature`: float within range [0.0, 50.0] °C\n    *   `humidity`: float within range [0.0, 100.0] %\n    *   `co2`: float within range [0.0, 1000.0] ppm\n    *   `light`: float within range [0.0, 2000.0] lux\n*   **Guardrail Alignment & Architectural Compliance**:\n    *   *No Tight Coupling*: Downstream clients consume a unified shape and unified abstract errors, preserving domain separation.\n    *   *No Secrets in Code*: The `PrivaClient` retrieves API keys dynamically via injected dictionary configurations, using harmless non-secret placeholders by default.\n    *   *Decisions Documented*: Key design vectors are codified inside the ADR directory structure.\n    *   *Validated Ingress*: Boundary violations or NaN representations immediately trigger structured `DataValidationError` exceptions.\n\nHere is the new execution result:\n\nTask: Continue Week 2 Phase 5 - Write integration tests for complete API workflow and coverage reporting.\n\nPhase 5 (after Phase 4):\n\n- qa-engineer: Write integration and API tests covering full workflow.\n  Output: tests/integration/test_end_to_end.py, tests/api/test_health.py, tests/api/test_upload.py, tests/api/test_inference.py, pytest.ini (updated), coverage_report.html\n  \n  Deliverables:\n  \n  1. tests/api/test_health.py\n     Health endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_health_endpoint_returns_ok\n       GET /health → status 200, body {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n     \n     - test_health_db_endpoint_connection_ok\n       GET /health/db → status 200, {\"status\": \"ok\", \"database\": \"connected\"}\n     \n     - test_health_db_endpoint_connection_fails\n       (Simulate DB down) → status 503, {\"status\": \"error\", \"database\": \"disconnected\"}\n     \n     - test_health_endpoint_no_auth_needed\n       No Authorization header → still returns 200\n  \n  2. tests/api/test_upload.py\n     CSV upload endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_upload_valid_csv\n       POST /api/upload with valid CSV\n       Expected: 200, {\"uploaded\": 1000, \"errors\": 0, ...}\n     \n     - test_upload_missing_tenant_id\n       POST without tenant_id\n       Expected: 400, error message\n     \n     - test_upload_invalid_csv_format\n       POST with malformed CSV (wrong columns)\n       Expected: 422, validation error\n     \n     - test_upload_nan_values\n       CSV with NaN in temperature column\n       Expected: 400 or 422 with error message\n     \n     - test_upload_out_of_range\n       Temperature = 55°C (max 50)\n       Expected: 400, validation error\n     \n     - test_upload_empty_file\n       POST with 0-byte CSV\n       Expected: 400, \"File is empty\"\n     \n     - test_upload_large_file\n       POST 100,000 rows CSV\n       Expected: 200, all rows uploaded\n     \n     - test_upload_data_persists\n       Upload CSV, query database\n       Expected: SensorReading entries created\n     \n     - test_upload_multi_tenant_isolation\n       Upload for tenant_1, then tenant_2\n       Query: tenant_1 should NOT see tenant_2's data\n       Expected: Proper filtering\n     \n     - test_upload_response_ranges\n       Check response has min/max for each sensor\n       Expected: ranges.temperature, ranges.humidity, etc. present\n  \n  3. tests/api/test_inference.py\n     Model inference endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_inference_returns_scores\n       POST /api/inference with sequences\n       Expected: 200, anomaly_scores array returned\n     \n     - test_inference_score_shape\n       Input 150 sequences → output 150 scores\n       Expected: len(anomaly_scores) == 150\n     \n     - test_inference_score_range\n       All scores in [0, 1]\n       Expected: min=0, max=1\n     \n     - test_inference_missing_tenant_id\n       POST without tenant_id\n       Expected: 400, error\n     \n     - test_inference_invalid_sequence_shape\n       POST with wrong sequence dimensions\n       Expected: 422, validation error\n     \n     - test_inference_nan_in_input\n       Input contains NaN\n       Expected: 400, validation error\n     \n     - test_inference_saves_to_database\n       Run inference, check anomaly_score column updated\n       Expected: SensorReading.anomaly_score populated\n     \n     - test_inference_model_not_found\n       (Simulate missing checkpoint)\n       Expected: 503, \"Model not loaded\"\n     \n     - test_inference_response_includes_high_anomalies\n       Response has high_anomalies field with flagged sequences\n       Expected: high_anomalies list present\n  \n  4. tests/integration/test_end_to_end.py\n     End-to-end workflow test:\n     \n     - test_csv_upload_to_inference_to_dashboard\n       \n       Step 1: Upload CSV via /api/upload\n         Input: 1000 rows sensor data (CSV file)\n         Expected: 200, 1000 uploaded\n       \n       Step 2: Verify data in database\n         Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sensor_reading\n         Expected: count >= 1000\n       \n       Step 3: Run inference via /api/inference\n         Input: sequences from uploaded data\n         Expected: 200, anomaly scores\n       \n       Step 4: Verify scores in database\n         Query: SELECT * WHERE anomaly_score IS NOT NULL\n         Expected: scores populated\n       \n       Step 5: Query dashboard data\n         GET from database (what dashboard uses)\n         Expected: data ready for visualization\n       \n       Step 6: Check multi-tenant isolation\n         Create tenant_1 and tenant_2 data\n         Query as tenant_1\n         Expected: Only see tenant_1's data\n     \n     - test_workflow_with_vendor_adapter\n       Use CSVAdapter.fetch_data() instead of raw CSV\n       Expected: Same results, vendor abstraction works\n     \n     - test_error_recovery\n       Upload invalid CSV → error → upload valid CSV → success\n       Expected: Second upload succeeds (no leftover state)\n  \n  5. pytest.ini (UPDATED)\n     Configuration:\n     \n     [pytest]\n     testpaths = tests\n     python_files = test_*.py\n     python_classes = Test*\n     python_functions = test_*\n     markers =\n         unit: Unit tests\n         integration: Integration tests\n         api: API endpoint tests\n         slow: Slow tests (skipped by default)\n         requires_db: Tests requiring database\n     \n     addopts = \n         -v\n         --tb=short\n         --cov=src\n         --cov-report=html:htmlcov\n         --cov-report=term-missing\n         --cov-fail-under=85\n         --strict-markers\n  \n  6. Coverage report:\n     Run: pytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n     Verify:\n       - src/api/ >85% coverage\n       - src/db/ >85% coverage\n       - src/vendors/ >85% coverage\n       - src/models/inference.py >85% coverage\n     \n     Generate: htmlcov/index.html (viewable in browser)\n  \n  Test fixtures needed:\n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_client():\n      FastAPI TestClient for endpoint testing\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def sample_csv_file(tmp_path):\n      Create valid CSV in temp directory\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_database():\n      Create in-memory SQLite for tests\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_sequences():\n      Generate 150 valid (20, 4) sequences\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def multiple_tenants(test_database):\n      Create test data for tenant_1, tenant_2, tenant_3\n  \n  Requirements:\n  - All tests pass: pytest tests/ -v\n  - Coverage >= 85% on new code\n  - Integration test covers full CSV → inference → dashboard workflow\n  - Multi-tenant isolation tested\n  - Error cases covered (invalid input, missing fields, etc.)\n  - No hardcoded paths (use fixtures, config)\n\nauto-proceed\nBuilt files:\n- [x] coverage_report.html\nFailed files:\n\n\nReturn the updated AGENT_MEMORY.md file content.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Here is the current memory:\n\n# Agent Memory\n\nThis document summarises the current stage, completed accomplishments, pending actions, and technical constraints of the Antigravity Agent (Code Reviewer & Quality Engineer).\n\n## Current Phase\nWe are currently executing **Week 2, Phase 4**: implementing and validating the Vendor Abstraction Layer, building the Priva API Client Stub, and delivering robust, comprehensive unit and end-to-end API test suites.\n\n## Completed Tasks\n*   **API Health Endpoint Test Overhaul ([tests/api/test_health.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_health.py))**:\n    *   Rewrote the broken health check tests to target 100% logic coverage of `/health` and `/health/db` routes in the API route definition.\n    *   Resolved severe integration/import bugs in the existing test layout: fixed the broken `from src.main import app` import to `from src.api.main import app`.\n    *   Corrected the invalid mock targets in database health-check testing: replaced `@patch('src.api.endpoints.health.get_db_session')` with FastAPI `dependency_overrides` on `get_db` to properly simulate real-world service injection.\n    *   Implemented exhaustive error path coverage: simulated standard successful connections, SQLite database locking failures (`SQLAlchemyError`), and general unhandled system exceptions (`Exception`).\n    *   Verified critical middleware functionality: validated CORS access control headers for stream applications, custom tracing correlation injection via `X-Request-ID` headers, and process timers.\n    *   Ensured authorization-free access validation on health endpoints.\n*   **Abstract Abstraction Design (`src/vendors/base.py`)**: Implemented the `DataSourceAdapter` interface mapping raw inputs to standard, multi-tenant schemas. Integrated custom hierarchical exceptions (`VendorError`, `DataSourceConnectionError`, `DataReadError`, `NormalizationError`, `DataValidationError`) and standard-validated columns.\n*   **CSV Adapter Implementation (`src/vendors/csv_adapter.py`)**: Formulated CSV-parsing mechanisms that ingest timezone-naive and timezone-aware timestamps, perform data range bound validations, and output pristine canonical columns.\n*   **Priva API Client Scaffold (`src/vendors/priva_client.py`)**: Engineered a concrete client stub enabling authentication hook scaffold (`_authenticate`), greenhouse polling (`_list_greenhouses`), and sensor reads (`_get_sensor_data`) with high-fidelity simulated response payloads matching our target sensor structure.\n*   **Comprehensive Testing Suite (`tests/vendors/`)**: Completed full test automation across happy/unhappy and boundary exception states:\n    *   [test_csv_adapter.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/vendors/test_csv_adapter.py) covers initialization, parsing of missing or invalid columns, non-numeric values, and empty structures.\n    *   [test_priva_stub.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/vendors/test_priva_stub.py) validates compliance to the interface, mock fetching, boundary validations, and method contracts.\n*   **Architecture & Quality Audit Documentation**:\n    *   Produced a code review report detailing structural and quality assessments for the source files.\n    *   Documented system architecture decisions in:\n        *   [ADR-001: Vendor Abstraction Layer](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-001-architecture.md)\n        *   [ADR-002: Synthetic Data Generation](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-002-synthetic-data.md)\n        *   [ADR-003: Modular Architecture](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-architecture.md)\n    *   Generated [week1-review.md](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/review/week1-review.md) summarizing foundational status.\n\n## Pending/Next Steps\n*   **Orchestration Support**: Integrate the newly minted `DataSourceAdapter` implementations directly with the main ingest pipeline and model training orchestration layers.\n*   **Dynamic Source Selection**: Allow quick switching between \"csv\" and \"priva\" ingestion based on tenant configuration settings without code modifications.\n*   **OAuth / Real Endpoint Upgrades (Phase 1.5)**: Replace mockup methods in `PrivaClient` with active network endpoints.\n*   **Run All Tests & Confirm Coverage**: Run coverage reports locally or in CI continuously to maintain >90% coverage goals constraints.\n\n## Technical Notes\n*   **Bugs Discovered & Reported**:\n    *   *Bug in existing `/health` test suite*: The legacy [tests/api/test_health.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_health.py) contained broken import references (`from src.main import app` instead of `from src.api.main import app`) and attempted to patch a non-existent module function `src.api.endpoints.health.get_db_session` instead of using FastAPI's standard dependency injection override mechanism, causing test discovery to fail. Overwritten with fully corrected and robust tests.\n*   **Canonical Sensor Schema**:\n    *   `timestamp`: timezone-aware datetime64 formatted in UTC\n    *   `temperature`: float within range [0.0, 50.0] °C\n    *   `humidity`: float within range [0.0, 100.0] %\n    *   `co2`: float within range [0.0, 1000.0] ppm\n    *   `light`: float within range [0.0, 2000.0] lux\n*   **Guardrail Alignment & Architectural Compliance**:\n    *   *No Tight Coupling*: Downstream clients consume a unified shape and unified abstract errors, preserving domain separation.\n    *   *No Secrets in Code*: The `PrivaClient` retrieves API keys dynamically via injected dictionary configurations, using harmless non-secret placeholders by default.\n    *   *Decisions Documented*: Key design vectors are codified inside the ADR directory structure.\n    *   *Validated Ingress*: Boundary violations or NaN representations immediately trigger structured `DataValidationError` exceptions.\n\nHere is the new execution result:\n\nTask: Continue Week 2 Phase 5 - Write integration tests for complete API workflow and coverage reporting.\n\nPhase 5 (after Phase 4):\n\n- qa-engineer: Write integration and API tests covering full workflow.\n  Output: tests/integration/test_end_to_end.py, tests/api/test_health.py, tests/api/test_upload.py, tests/api/test_inference.py, pytest.ini (updated), coverage_report.html\n  \n  Deliverables:\n  \n  1. tests/api/test_health.py\n     Health endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_health_endpoint_returns_ok\n       GET /health → status 200, body {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n     \n     - test_health_db_endpoint_connection_ok\n       GET /health/db → status 200, {\"status\": \"ok\", \"database\": \"connected\"}\n     \n     - test_health_db_endpoint_connection_fails\n       (Simulate DB down) → status 503, {\"status\": \"error\", \"database\": \"disconnected\"}\n     \n     - test_health_endpoint_no_auth_needed\n       No Authorization header → still returns 200\n  \n  2. tests/api/test_upload.py\n     CSV upload endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_upload_valid_csv\n       POST /api/upload with valid CSV\n       Expected: 200, {\"uploaded\": 1000, \"errors\": 0, ...}\n     \n     - test_upload_missing_tenant_id\n       POST without tenant_id\n       Expected: 400, error message\n     \n     - test_upload_invalid_csv_format\n       POST with malformed CSV (wrong columns)\n       Expected: 422, validation error\n     \n     - test_upload_nan_values\n       CSV with NaN in temperature column\n       Expected: 400 or 422 with error message\n     \n     - test_upload_out_of_range\n       Temperature = 55°C (max 50)\n       Expected: 400, validation error\n     \n     - test_upload_empty_file\n       POST with 0-byte CSV\n       Expected: 400, \"File is empty\"\n     \n     - test_upload_large_file\n       POST 100,000 rows CSV\n       Expected: 200, all rows uploaded\n     \n     - test_upload_data_persists\n       Upload CSV, query database\n       Expected: SensorReading entries created\n     \n     - test_upload_multi_tenant_isolation\n       Upload for tenant_1, then tenant_2\n       Query: tenant_1 should NOT see tenant_2's data\n       Expected: Proper filtering\n     \n     - test_upload_response_ranges\n       Check response has min/max for each sensor\n       Expected: ranges.temperature, ranges.humidity, etc. present\n  \n  3. tests/api/test_inference.py\n     Model inference endpoint tests:\n     \n     - test_inference_returns_scores\n       POST /api/inference with sequences\n       Expected: 200, anomaly_scores array returned\n     \n     - test_inference_score_shape\n       Input 150 sequences → output 150 scores\n       Expected: len(anomaly_scores) == 150\n     \n     - test_inference_score_range\n       All scores in [0, 1]\n       Expected: min=0, max=1\n     \n     - test_inference_missing_tenant_id\n       POST without tenant_id\n       Expected: 400, error\n     \n     - test_inference_invalid_sequence_shape\n       POST with wrong sequence dimensions\n       Expected: 422, validation error\n     \n     - test_inference_nan_in_input\n       Input contains NaN\n       Expected: 400, validation error\n     \n     - test_inference_saves_to_database\n       Run inference, check anomaly_score column updated\n       Expected: SensorReading.anomaly_score populated\n     \n     - test_inference_model_not_found\n       (Simulate missing checkpoint)\n       Expected: 503, \"Model not loaded\"\n     \n     - test_inference_response_includes_high_anomalies\n       Response has high_anomalies field with flagged sequences\n       Expected: high_anomalies list present\n  \n  4. tests/integration/test_end_to_end.py\n     End-to-end workflow test:\n     \n     - test_csv_upload_to_inference_to_dashboard\n       \n       Step 1: Upload CSV via /api/upload\n         Input: 1000 rows sensor data (CSV file)\n         Expected: 200, 1000 uploaded\n       \n       Step 2: Verify data in database\n         Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sensor_reading\n         Expected: count >= 1000\n       \n       Step 3: Run inference via /api/inference\n         Input: sequences from uploaded data\n         Expected: 200, anomaly scores\n       \n       Step 4: Verify scores in database\n         Query: SELECT * WHERE anomaly_score IS NOT NULL\n         Expected: scores populated\n       \n       Step 5: Query dashboard data\n         GET from database (what dashboard uses)\n         Expected: data ready for visualization\n       \n       Step 6: Check multi-tenant isolation\n         Create tenant_1 and tenant_2 data\n         Query as tenant_1\n         Expected: Only see tenant_1's data\n     \n     - test_workflow_with_vendor_adapter\n       Use CSVAdapter.fetch_data() instead of raw CSV\n       Expected: Same results, vendor abstraction works\n     \n     - test_error_recovery\n       Upload invalid CSV → error → upload valid CSV → success\n       Expected: Second upload succeeds (no leftover state)\n  \n  5. pytest.ini (UPDATED)\n     Configuration:\n     \n     [pytest]\n     testpaths = tests\n     python_files = test_*.py\n     python_classes = Test*\n     python_functions = test_*\n     markers =\n         unit: Unit tests\n         integration: Integration tests\n         api: API endpoint tests\n         slow: Slow tests (skipped by default)\n         requires_db: Tests requiring database\n     \n     addopts = \n         -v\n         --tb=short\n         --cov=src\n         --cov-report=html:htmlcov\n         --cov-report=term-missing\n         --cov-fail-under=85\n         --strict-markers\n  \n  6. Coverage report:\n     Run: pytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\n     Verify:\n       - src/api/ >85% coverage\n       - src/db/ >85% coverage\n       - src/vendors/ >85% coverage\n       - src/models/inference.py >85% coverage\n     \n     Generate: htmlcov/index.html (viewable in browser)\n  \n  Test fixtures needed:\n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_client():\n      FastAPI TestClient for endpoint testing\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def sample_csv_file(tmp_path):\n      Create valid CSV in temp directory\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_database():\n      Create in-memory SQLite for tests\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def test_sequences():\n      Generate 150 valid (20, 4) sequences\n    \n  - @pytest.fixture\n    def multiple_tenants(test_database):\n      Create test data for tenant_1, tenant_2, tenant_3\n  \n  Requirements:\n  - All tests pass: pytest tests/ -v\n  - Coverage >= 85% on new code\n  - Integration test covers full CSV → inference → dashboard 