ut/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEKLY-SYNC-CONTEXT)\n# Weekly Sync Context Handover\nhandover_id: \"weekly-sync\"\nname: \"Weekly Sync Context\"\ndescription: \"Passing context from one week to agents for next week\"\n\ntrigger: \"Friday end of week\"\n\ntemplate: |\n  Team sync context:\n\n  Week [N] Progress:\n  - ML Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - Backend Engineer: [What was accomplished]\n  - DevOps Lead: [What was accomplished]\n  - Architect: [Assessment of week]\n\n  Metrics:\n  - Model accuracy: [X]%\n  - API latency: [X]ms\n  - Test coverage: [X]%\n  - Infrastructure status: [Status]\n\n  Blockers:\n  - [Blocker 1]\n  - [Blocker 2]\n\n  Week [N+1] Focus:\n  - ML Engineer will: [Task]\n  - Backend Engineer will: [Task]\n  - DevOps Lead will: [Task]\n  - Architect will: [Task]\n\n  Questions for next week:\n  - [Question 1]\n  - [Question 2]\n\nagents_to_receive:\n  - \"ml-engineer\"\n  - \"backend-engineer\"\n  - \"devops-lead\"\n  - \"architect\"\n\ntiming: \"Monday morning before work starts\"\n</agent_context>\n\nTASK: Review the anomaly detection preprocessing, sequence parsing, and tensor scaling implemented in the `run_inference_from_csv` function within `src/api/routes/inference.py`. Assess the correctness and efficiency of the machine learning logic. Document your findings and recommendations in the output file.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: ml_review.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agen