2026-06-09 14:50:11,989 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"122","timestampMicros":"1781013011989370","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"a025b31c506ad65eaa33b389dfd7f82e","trajectoryId":"a025b31c506ad65eaa33b389dfd7f82e","stepIndex":28,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Code review document creation","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/be_review.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":0,"lines":[{"text":"# Backend Engineering Code Review: FastAPI Ingestion & Inference Layers","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"This document presents a comprehensive review of the FastAPI route logic in [inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py) and [upload.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/upload.py). The review evaluates these routes against robustness, error handling, performance benchmarks, memory leak hazards, and architectural alignment as defined in the Week 2 Backend Guidelines and project constraints.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"---","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## 🛑 Blockers (Immediate Action Required)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 1. Tight-Coupling of ML Post-Processing inside FastAPI Routes","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"In [inference.py:L50-51](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py#L50-L51) and [L156-157](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py#L156-L157), VAE model raw reconstruction error scaling and clipping are implemented directly within the routing layer:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(...)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / 2.0, 0.0, 1.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** The dividing divisor (`2.0`) and clipping range (`0.0` to `1.0`) are mathematical post-processing heuristics. Hardcoding them in the API tier violates the **Loose Coupling** guardrail. If model configuration parameters change (such as hidden dimension scales or the beta divergence ratio), the reconstruction scores scale shifts, and the backend routes must be modified to prevent incorrect scaling or clipping.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** Structural coupling breaks modularity between the ML model and the delivery API.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Move this scoring heuristic inside `AnomalyDetector.predict_batch` or a model post-processor class so the route layer only deals with finalized, scaled `[0..1]` scores.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 2. Unbounded Memory Leak in Model Caching (`_model_cache`)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"In [inference.py:L12](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py#L12) and [L35-46](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py#L35-L46), loaded VAE models are cached indefinitely in a class-level dictionary:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"_model_cache: Dict[str, LSTMVAE] = {}","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** There is no cache eviction strategy (like Least-Recently-Used or TTL pruning). Over time, in a multi-tenant setup where dynamically-trained tenant-specific models (checkpoints) are reloaded across hundreds or thousands of clients, this cache will grow unbounded.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** This will cause a progressive memory leak, eventually triggering server-wide container Out Of Memory (OOM) fatal crashes.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Integrate `cachetools.LRUCache` or a simple queue-based size constraint (e.g., maximum 10 models in memory, evicting the oldest) inside `AnomalyDetector`'s model loader.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 3. Blind Temporal Index Matching & Race Condition in Score Persist","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"In [inference.py:L58-76](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py#L58-L76), anomaly scores are matched and persisted back to the database purely based on sequence lists and index limits:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"stmt = select(SensorReading).where(","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    SensorReading.tenant_id == request.tenant_id,","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    SensorReading.greenhouse_id == request.greenhouse_id,","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":").order_by(SensorReading.timestamp.desc()).limit(len(batch_scores))","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"...","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"for idx, record in enumerate(reversed(records)):","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    if idx < len(batch_scores):","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        record.anomaly_score = float(batch_scores[idx])","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** Timestamps or unique reading identifiers of the incoming sequence array are not compared against the database records! The code assumes the latest database entries perfectly correspond to the array elements.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** ","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  1. If a client transmits historical data or out-of-order sequences, wrong anomaly scores will be written to random database rows.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  2. If the DB contains fewer records than the request batch size ($K < \\text{len}(scores)$), the database update fails silently for the trailing scores.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  3. Under concurrent uploads, standard race conditions will result in database entries receiving completely mismatched scores.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Expose specific record IDs or explicit timestamps in the `InferenceRequest` body, and utilize a targeted bulk update query with exact matches instead of sliding index assumptions.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 4. Excessive In-Memory Allocations during CSV Upload (Scale Memory Leak)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"In [upload.py:L25-27](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/upload.py#L25-L27) and [inference.py:L110](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py#L110), file contents are read entirely into memory as raw bytes, decoded to unicode strings, and loaded as full Pandas DataFrames:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"content = await file.read()","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"df = pd.read_csv(StringIO(content.decode(\"utf-8\")))","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** Reading large uploaded bulk files directly into RAM creates a triple-copy allocation peak (raw bytes + decoded unicode string + String IO buffers + parsed DataFrame objects).","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** If a vendor attempts a bulk historics upload of 50M-100MB, the server RAM usage spikes by 500M-1GB, causing massive latency bottlenecks or OOM aborts.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Stream the file chunks to a temporary filesystem path (`tempfile`), or process the stream in batches using pandas' `chunksize` parameters. Ensure file unlinking in `inference.py` is safely wrapped in `try...finally` boundaries.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 5. RAM Spill via Thick SQLAlchemy ORM Object Instantiation","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"In [upload.py:L58-71](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/upload.py#L58-L71), bulk CSV records are iterated, individual Python objects are initialized, and tracked via session:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"records = []","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"for _, row in df.iterrows():","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    reading = SensorReading(...)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    records.append(reading)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"db.add_all(records)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** Generating individual thick SQLAlchemy ORM instances for thousands of CSV readings forces the AsyncSession identity map to maintain full state tracking, dirty-checks, and session reference markers for thousands of Python objects.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** Memory spills inside the active thread and bulk inserts are exceptionally sluggish.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Utilize standard SQLAlchemy 2.0 Core bulk inserts to completely bypass ORM state tracking overhead:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  ```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  from sqlalchemy import insert","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  # Prepare a fast payload list of raw dicts","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  records_dict = df.to_dict(orient=\"records\")","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  await db.execute(insert(SensorReading), records_dict)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  ```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"---","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## ⚠️ Warnings (Areas to Improve)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 1. Vendor Abstraction Layer Bypass & Severe Code Duplication","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** The specialized [CSVAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/csv_adapter.py) engineering in Week 2 was specifically designed to handle CSV uploads, parse inputs, standardise column sets, validate types, and convert timezone-naive timestamps to timezone-aware UTC format. Yet, [upload.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/upload.py) completely bypasses `CSVAdapter`, manually duplicating Pandas CSV parsers, checking column subsets, and validating limits directly in the route file.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** Violates modular separation of concerns and creates duplicated parsing points. If the csv model schema layout changes, both the adapter and the endpoint routes must be manually updated.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Refactor `/upload` in `upload.py` to ingest and process data directly through `CSVAdapter`.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 2. Timezone Loss on Insertion (Data Inconsistencies)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** The physical database column `SensorReading.timestamp` is designated as `DateTime(timezone=True)`. However, `/upload` parses dates with `pd.to_datetime(df['timestamp'])` which strips timezone markers, producing timezone-naive timestamps.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** SQLite silently accepts raw timezone-naive inserts. Over time, when queries convert readings or filter them, timezone discrepancies skew historical graphs by hours.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Enforce UTC conversion. Relying on `CSVAdapter.get_data()` automatically enforces and converts all timestamps into pristine timezone-aware UTC structures.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### 3. Hardcoded Physical Boundary Thresholds","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **The Issue:** Physical limit bounds of numerical variables in `/upload` lines 40-47 are hard-coded directly as raw numeric literals `(0, 50)`, `(0, 100)`, `(0, 1000)`, `(0, 2000)` inside the route.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Consequence:** This violates backend development instructions: *\"Hard-coded thresholds should be in src/config.py — WARN\"*.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **📝 Recommendation:** Centralize physical canonical boundaries into `src/config.py` as globally shared constants, importing them into schemas and validators alike, as follows:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  ```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  CANONICAL_TEMP_LIMITS = (0.0, 50.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  CANONICAL_HUMID_LIMITS = (0.0, 100.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  CANONICAL_CO2_LIMITS = (0.0, 1000.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  CANONICAL_LIGHT_LIMITS = (0.0, 2000.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"  ```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"---","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## ✅ Quality, Schema & Documentation Pass Audit","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Type Hints:** Both modules contain full python type hinting across functions, return payloads, and FastAPI dependency annotations (`AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)`).","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Docstrings:** High quality and complete function descriptors detailing input and schema specifications.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Pydantic Validation (Ingress Layer):** The API schemas are correctly authored in **Pydantic v2** conventions. High-quality tensor validation rules in `InferenceRequest` successfully block mismatched matrices (`seq_len != 20` or `input_dim != 4`) early before reaching PyTorch space.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **DB Guardrail Compliance:** All schema operations query and filter by the mandatory multi-tenant field `tenant_id` consistently, aligning with strict security requirements.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"---","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"## 🚀 Recommended Action Plan","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### Step 1: Encapsulate Scoring Scale to Resolve Tight-Coupling","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Modify `AnomalyDetector.predict` or `predict_batch` inside [src/models/inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py) to integrate raw scaling and clipping internally:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"# Inside AnomalyDetector:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"def predict_batch(self, sequences: List[np.ndarray]) -> np.ndarray:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    stacked = np.stack(sequences)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    raw_scores = self.predict(stacked)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    # Scaled and clipped post-processing encapsulated safely inside the model wrapper","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    return np.clip(raw_scores / 2.0, 0.0, 1.0)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"This cleans up [inference.py:L51](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py#L51) and avoids machine learning heuristic exposure in the routing layer.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### Step 2: Implement LRU Eviction in Model Cache","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Import and utilize `cachetools` or restrict size dynamically:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"# Inside AnomalyDetector:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"def _load_model(self) -> LSTMVAE:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    if len(self._model_cache) > 10:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        # Evict oldest loaded model to limit RAM footprint","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        first_key = next(iter(self._model_cache))","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        self._model_cache.pop(first_key)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    ...","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"### Step 3: Refactor CSV Upload route to use `CSVAdapter` and SQLAlchemy Core Bulk Ingest","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"Replace manual pandas operations in `upload.py` with the robust `CSVAdapter` workflow:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```python","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"# Refactored upload.py snippet:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"@router.post(\"/upload\", response_model=UploadResponse)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"async def upload_csv(","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    file: UploadFile = File(...),","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    tenant_id: str = Form(...),","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    greenhouse_id: str = Form(\"default\"),","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"):","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    if not file.filename.endswith('.csv'):","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Only CSV files are supported\")","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    content = await file.read()","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    ","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    # Process through the specialized CSV Adapter safely","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=\".csv\") as tmp:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        tmp.write(content)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        tmp_path = tmp.name","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    try:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        adapter = CSVAdapter({\"filepath\": tmp_path})","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        df = adapter.get_data() # Validates, UTC converts, and converts schemas cleanly!","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    except Exception as e:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=f\"Data pipeline validation failed: {str(e)}\")","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    finally:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        if os.path.exists(tmp_path):","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            os.unlink(tmp_path)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    # Core bulk insert to bypass individual ORM object overhead","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    records_dict = []","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    for _, row in df.iterrows():","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        records_dict.append({","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"tenant_id\": tenant_id,","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id,","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"timestamp\": row['timestamp'].to_pydatetime(),","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"temperature\": row['temperature'],","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"humidity\": row['humidity'],","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"co2\": row['co2'],","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"            \"light\": row['light']","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        })","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    from sqlalchemy import insert","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    try:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        await db.execute(insert(SensorReading), records_dict)","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        await db.commit()","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"    except Exception as e:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        await db.rollback()","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Database persistent error: {str(e)}\")","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"```","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"}]}]}}}
