alized that processing chunks independently leads to a loss of sequences at the boundaries. To resolve this, I'm now implementing a method to prepend the last `seq_len - 1` rows of the previous chunk to the current chunk. This ensures complete sequences are generated, regardless of the chunk boundaries, and all data is processed correctly. This will prevent loss in high-anomaly scenarios and will yield accurate scoring and detection.\n\n\n","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"**Implementing Cross-Chunk Overlap**\n\nI've been working on a solution to handle sequence windowing across CSV upload chunk boundaries. I realized that processing chunks independently leads to a loss of sequences at the boundaries. To resolve this, I'm now implementing a method to prepend the last `seq_len - 1` rows of the previous chunk to the current chunk. This ensures complete sequences are generated, regardless of the chunk boundaries, and all data is processed correctly. This will prevent loss in high-anomaly scenarios and will yield accurate scoring and detection.\n\n\n","text":""}}
