nt of timestamps with anomaly scores during sequence windowing. I've realized that sequence anomaly scores $N$ are less than $T$ (number of raw data rows), because $N = T - seq\\_len + 1$. Aligning each score to the *last* element index ensures a precise mapping; hence, I've re-evaluated that we need to slice the timestamps from index `seq_len - 1` to match the exact length of the anomaly scores, using a sliding window. It's mathematically sound, and aligns perfectly with standard sliding window timestamp alignment. I'm building it, now.\n\n\n","text":""}}
