2026-06-09 15:06:44,327 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"2","timestampMicros":"1781014004327454","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"d1249288d6b7ecc64a608a0df44e5673","trajectoryId":"d1249288d6b7ecc64a608a0df44e5673","stepIndex":0,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_USER","target":"TARGET_MODEL","thinking":"","textDelta":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== ml-engineer output ===\n# ML Engineer Changes\n\nThis file documents the changes made by the ML Engineer to decouple post-processing logic from the inference API route.\n\n## 1. Created `src/models/postprocessing.py`\n\nA new file was created to house the post-processing logic.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List\n\ndef map_timestamp_to_anomaly(\n    timestamps: pd.Series, reconstruction_error: np.ndarray, threshold: float\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Maps timestamps to detected anomalies based on reconstruction error.\"\"\"\n    anomalies = pd.DataFrame(\n        {\"timestamp\": timestamps, \"reconstruction_error\": reconstruction_error.flatten()}\n    )\n    return anomalies[anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"] > threshold]\n\ndef clip_and_scale_anomalies(\n    anomalies: pd.DataFrame, scaling_factor: float\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Clips anomaly scores and scales them for visualization.\"\"\"\n    anomalies[\"clipped_error\"] = np.clip(anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"], 0, None)\n    anomalies[\"scaled_error\"] = anomalies[\"clipped_error\"] * scaling_factor\n    return anomalies\n\ndef get_high_anomaly_timestamps(\n    anomalies: pd.DataFrame, threshold: float\n) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Filters for high-severity anomalies and returns a list of dictionaries.\"\"\"\n    high_anomalies = anomalies[anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"] > threshold]\n    return high_anomalies.to_dict(\"records\")\n```\n\n## 2. Updated `src/config.py`\n\nThe configuration file was updated to include new parameters for anomaly detection.\n\n```python\n# =============================================================================\n# Anomaly Detection and Post-Processing\n# =============================================================================\nANOMALY_THRESHOLD: float = 0.8\nANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR: float = 2.0\n```\n\n## 3. Updated `src/api/routes/inference.py`\n\nThe inference route was updated to use the new post-processing functions and configuration values.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Depends\nfrom src.api.schemas.sensor_data import InferenceRequest, InferenceResponse\nfrom src.db.session import get_db\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.future import select\nfrom src.db.models import SensorReading\nfrom src.models.inference import AnomalyDetector\nfrom src.models.model_registry import ModelRegistry\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport numpy as np\nfrom fastapi import UploadFile, File, Form\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\nfrom src.vendors.csv_adapter import CSVAdapter\nfrom src.models.data_utils import preprocess_sequences, normalize_data, SENSOR_RANGES\nfrom src.models.postprocessing import (\n    map_timestamp_to_anomaly,\n    clip_and_scale_anomalies,\n    get_high_anomaly_timestamps,\n)\nfrom src.config import ANOMALY_THRESHOLD, ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\n@router.post(\"/inference\", response_model=InferenceResponse)\nasync def run_inference(\n    request: InferenceRequest,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    seqs = request.sequences\n    if not seqs:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Empty sequences\")\n\n    # Resolve active model for customer\n    registry = ModelRegistry(db)\n    active_model_info = await registry.get_active_model(request.tenant_id)\n\n    checkpoint_path = None\n    model_id_used = \"baseline_v1\"\n\n    if active_model_info:\n        checkpoint_path = active_model_info[\"checkpoint_path\"]\n        model_id_used = active_model_info[\"model_id\"]\n\n    try:\n        detector = AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=f\"Failed to initialize model: {e}\")\n\n    try:\n        # Expected shape (batch, seq_len, input_dim) -> (batch, 20, 4)\n        np_seqs = [np.array(seq, dtype=np.float32) for seq in seqs]\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(np_seqs)\n        # Scale or clip raw reconstruction errors to [0, 1] range to satisfy Pydantic Schema\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Inference failed: {str(e)}\")\n\n    anomalies_detected = int((batch_scores > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD).sum())\n    high_anomalies = [\n        {\"sequence_index\": i, \"score\": float(s), \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\n        for i, s in enumerate(batch_scores)\n        if s > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n    ]\n\n    # Persist scores to the matching database records for this tenant/greenhouse\n    stmt = select(SensorReading).where(\n        SensorReading.tenant_id == request.tenant_id,\n        SensorReading.greenhouse_id == request.greenhouse_id,\n    ).order_by(SensorReading.timestamp.desc()).limit(len(batch_scores))\n\n    result = await db.execute(stmt)\n    records = result.scalars().all()\n\n    # We update records with anomaly scores starting from the matching indices\n    for idx, record in enumerate(reversed(records)):\n        if idx < len(batch_scores):\n            record.anomaly_score = float(batch_scores[idx])\n\n    try:\n        await db.commit()\n    except Exception as e:\n        await db.rollback()\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Failed to persist anomaly scores: {str(e)}\")\n\n    return InferenceResponse(\n        tenant_id=request.tenant_id,\n        greenhouse_id=request.greenhouse_id,\n        sequences_processed=len(seqs),\n        anomalies_detected=anomalies_detected,\n        anomaly_scores=batch_scores.tolist(),\n        high_anomalies=high_anomalies\n    )\n\n\n@router.post(\"/inference/upload\")\nasync def run_inference_from_csv(\n    tenant_id: str = Form(...),\n    greenhouse_id: str = Form(default=\"default\"),\n    file: UploadFile = File(...),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Directly runs inference on an uploaded CSV file without persisting the raw data,\n    returning the anomaly scores and a list of high anomaly items.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not file.filename.endswith(\".csv\"):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Only CSV files are supported.\")\n\n    content = await file.read()\n\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=\".csv\") as tmp:\n        tmp.write(content)\n        tmp_path = tmp.name\n\n    try:\n        adapter = CSVAdapter({\"filepath\": tmp_path})\n        df = adapter.get_data()\n    except Exception as e:\n        os.unlink(tmp_path)\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=f\"Invalid CSV format: {e}\")\n\n    os.unlink(tmp_path)\n\n    if df.empty:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Uploaded CSV contains no valid data.\")\n\n    # Extract required columns for inference: temperature, humidity, co2, light\n    try:\n        raw_data = df[[\"temperature\", \"humidity\", \"co2\", \"light\"]].to_numpy()\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=f\"Missing required columns: {e}\")\n\n    # Normalize data using standard ranges\n    norm_data = normalize_data(raw_data, SENSOR_RANGES)\n\n    try:\n        sequences = preprocess_sequences(norm_data, seq_len=20)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(e))\n\n    # Resolve active model for customer\n    registry = ModelRegistry(db)\n    active_model_info = await registry.get_active_model(tenant_id)\n\n    checkpoint_path = None\n    if active_model_info:\n        checkpoint_path = active_model_info[\"checkpoint_path\"]\n\n    try:\n        detector = AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=f\"Failed to initialize model: {e}\")\n\n    try:\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(sequences)\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Inference failed: {str(e)}\")\n\n    anomalies_detected = int((batch_scores > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD).sum())\n\n    anomalies_df = map_timestamp_to_anomaly(\n        df[\"timestamp\"], batch_scores, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n    )\n\n    high_anomalies = get_high_anomaly_timestamps(anomalies_df, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD)\n\n    return {\n        \"tenant_id\": tenant_id,\n        \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id,\n        \"sequences_processed\": len(sequences),\n        \"anomalies_detected\": anomalies_detected,\n        \"anomaly_scores\": batch_scores.tolist(),\n        \"high_anomalies\": high_anomalies\n    }\n```\n\n\n=== backend-engineer output ===\n# Backend Optimization Report\n\nThis report outlines the structural enhancements made to the FastAPI backend model inference and upload layers of the AI Agronomist platform. The optimizations guarantee multi-tenant memory safety, robust sliding window math, and model caching with thread-safe limits.\n\n## 🛠️ Summary of Accomplishments\n\n### 1. Memory-Safe Chunked Upload Ingestion (`/api/inference/upload`)\n\n- **Problem**: The old `/api/inference/upload` endpoint performed `file.read()`, holding the entire uploaded file in memory as a giant byte string. It then parsed the database frame all at once via `CSVAdapter.get_data()`. Running model sequences on massive files (e.g., hundreds of megabytes) caused high memory exhaustion and risking Out-of-Memory (OOM) process crashes.\n- **Refactor**:\n  - Implemented streamed buffering to save file bytes in 1MB chunks into a temporary file using `while chunk := await file.read(1024 * 1024):`.\n  - Employed Pandas `read_csv(..., chunksize=5000)` iterator to process the CSV in memory-efficient chunks of 5000 rows.\n  - Verified that each chunk is individually normalized and validated using the `CSVAdapter.normalize` and `CSVAdapter.validate` methods, failing early with a 422 standard HTTP status code if any chunk contains out-of-range sensor measurements, NaNs, or schema infractions.\n  - Ensures that regardless of the file size (from 1KB to multi-gigabytes), the process memory consumption remains tiny and constant.\n\n### 2. Robust Sliding Window Overlap & Timestamp Mapping\n\n- **Problem**: Sliding temporal window math (using `seq_len = 20`) requires groupings of 20 consecutive timestamps. If chunks of size 5000 are processed independently, 19 sequences spanning across chunk boundaries ($seq\\_len - 1$) would be completely discarded. Additionally, mapping anomaly scores to timestamps by aligning lists with different lengths directly results in `ValueError` and index mismatches.\n- **Refactor**:\n  - **Border-Overlap Prepending**: Created a state-carrying buffer `prev_overlap_df` that captures the last `seq_len - 1` (19) rows of each normalized chunk and prepends them onto the next chunk. This guarantees zero border-loss of sequence sliding windows at the chunk transitions.\n  - **Exact Timestamp Mapping**: Mapped each temporal sequence output score $i$ within a chunk back to the exact original timestamp of the end of its window (row $i + seq\\_len - 1$ of the chunk's virtual timeline).\n  - **Safety Bound Checks**: Added boundary safety guards (`if row_idx < len(timestamps):`) and handling for missing/NaT timestamps (resolved to `\"unknown\"`) to completely prevent index out of bounds exceptions. This guarantees 100% robust sequence index mapping.\n\n### 3. Thread-Safe LRU Model Caching\n\n- **Problem**: `AnomalyDetector` models were instantiated from scratch on every incoming request. This resulted in loading heavy PyTorch neural model weights (`LSTMVAE`) over and over, severely dragging request latencies down and filling memory with redundant weights (unbounded leakage).\n- **Refactor**:\n  - Introduced standard library thread-safe `@lru_cache(maxsize=16)` in `src/api/routes/inference.py` wrapping the `AnomalyDetector` factory function:\n    ```python\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=16)\n    def get_cached_detector(checkpoint_path: Optional[str]) -> AnomalyDetector:\n        return AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    ```\n  - Placed this cached detector factory into both `/api/inference` and `/api/inference/upload` routes. This ensures that when the same customer model or the baseline model is invoked, its weight parameters are re-used instantly, dropping API response time to single-digit milliseconds while bounding memory utilization to at most 16 unique active models.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Modified Files and Code Links\n\nThe modifications are cleanly confined within the backend route and test structures, strictly obeying modular ownership boundaries:\n\n1. **[src/api/routes/inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py)**:\n   - Added `get_cached_detector` with thread-safe `@lru_cache(maxsize=16)` to cache the [AnomalyDetector](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py) instance.\n   - Refactored [run_inference_from_csv](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py) to stream uploaded files chunk-by-chunk and validate/normalize via [CSVAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/csv_adapter.py) iteratively.\n   - Incorporated stateful `prev_overlap_df` logic to retain sliding window continuity.\n2. **[tests/api/test_inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_inference.py)**:\n   - Added [test_inference_upload_csv](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_inference.py) verifying that the refactored chunked CSV ingestion endpoint processes sequence batches correctly and maps sequence indices robustly to timestamps.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Code Walkthrough\n\n```python\n# Extract from /api/inference/upload in src/api/routes/inference.py\n@router.post(\"/inference/upload\")\nasync def run_inference_from_csv(\n    tenant_id: str = Form(...),\n    greenhouse_id: str = Form(default=\"default\"),\n    file: UploadFile = File(...),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    ...\n    # Stream-buffer the uploaded file into a temp file (O(1) memory footprint)\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=\".csv\") as tmp:\n        while chunk := await file.read(1024 * 1024):\n            tmp.write(chunk)\n        tmp_path = tmp.name\n\n    ...\n    # Read CSV in chunks\n    for raw_chunk in pd.read_csv(tmp_path, chunksize=5000):\n        # Normalize and validate chunk independently\n        normalized_chunk = adapter.normalize(raw_chunk)\n        adapter.validate(normalized_chunk)\n\n        # Concat with last chunk's overlap (retaining sliding sequence window math)\n        combined_df = pd.concat([prev_overlap_df, normalized_chunk], ignore_index=True)\n        prev_overlap_df = normalized_chunk.iloc[-(seq_len - 1):].copy()\n\n        ...\n        # Run predictions in mini batch\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(sequences)\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n        # Safe sliding index timestamp alignment\n        timestamps = combined_df[\"timestamp\"].tolist()\n        for idx, score in enumerate(batch_scores):\n            row_idx = idx + seq_len - 1\n            ts = timestamps[row_idx].isoformat() if row_idx < len(timestamps) else \"unknown\"\n            ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Guardrails & Compliance Check\n\n- **no_tight_coupling**: High compliance. The route layer consumes the unified API contract of [DataSourceAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/base.py) subclass [CSVAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/csv_adapter.py) and runs [AnomalyDetector](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py). Both ML and ingest internals are completely decoupled.\n- **canonical_schema**: High compliance. Standard numerical physical ranges ([temp_range](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/config.py#L87-L90), etc.) and column validations are enforced at every individual chunk level.\n- **no_secrets_in_code**: Verified. No credentials or authentication keys are saved inside source code.\n- **test_coverage**: Rigorous integration validations added. Both model cache reuse and large processing pipelines are robustly verified.\n\n\n=== tech-lead output ===\n# Tech Lead Changes\n\nThis file documents the changes made by the Tech Lead to improve the frontend validation and user feedback in the dashboard.\n\n## 1. Updated `src/dashboard/pages/5_upload_operations.py`\n\nThe dashboard page for upload operations was updated to:\n\n- Import `ANOMALY_THRESHOLD` from `src.config` to ensure consistency with the backend.\n- Add frontend validation to ensure that `Tenant ID` and `Greenhouse ID` are not empty before making API calls.\n- Correct the UI notification for model training to reflect its asynchronous nature.\n\n```python\nimport streamlit as st\nimport requests\nimport pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\nfrom src.config import API_URL, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n\nst.set_page_config(page_title=\"Upload & Operations\", page_icon=\"📤\", layout=\"wide\")\n\nst.title(\"Data Upload & Model Operations\")\nst.markdown(\"Upload raw sensor data for training or find anomalies instantly using the active model.\")\n\ntab1, tab2 = st.tabs([\"Upload & Train Model\", \"Upload & Find Anomalies\"])\n\nwith tab1:\n    st.header(\"Upload Data & Train Model\")\n    st.write(\"Ingest historical data into the platform and trigger a new model training cycle.\")\n\n    col1, col2 = st.columns(2)\n    with col1:\n        tenant_id_train = st.text_input(\"Tenant ID\", \"tenant_1\", key=\"tenant_train\")\n        greenhouse_id_train = st.text_input(\"Greenhouse ID\", \"default\", key=\"greenhouse_train\")\n\n    uploaded_file_train = st.file_uploader(\"Choose a CSV file for training\", type=\"csv\", key=\"file_train\")\n\n    if st.button(\"Upload & Train\", type=\"primary\"):\n        if not tenant_id_train or not greenhouse_id_train:\n            st.warning(\"Tenant ID and Greenhouse ID cannot be empty.\")\n        elif uploaded_file_train is not None:\n            with st.spinner(\"Uploading data to platform...\"):\n                files = {\"file\": (uploaded_file_train.name, uploaded_file_train.getvalue(), \"text/csv\")}\n                data = {\"tenant_id\": tenant_id_train, \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id_train}\n                try:\n                    res_upload = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/upload\", files=files, data=data)\n                    res_upload.raise_for_status()\n                    st.success(f\"Successfully uploaded {res_upload.json().get('uploaded', 0)} rows.\")\n\n                    st.info(\"Triggering model training pipeline...\")\n                    res_train = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/models/{tenant_id_train}/train\")\n                    res_train.raise_for_status()\n                    st.success(\"Training dispatched in the background.\")\n                    st.json(res_train.json())\n                except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n                    st.error(f\"Operation failed: {e}\")\n                    if hasattr(e, 'response') and e.response is not None:\n                        try:\n                            st.json(e.response.json())\n                        except Exception:\n                            st.write(e.response.text)\n        else:\n            st.warning(\"Please upload a CSV file first.\")\n\nwith tab2:\n    st.header(\"Upload & Find Anomalies\")\n    st.write(\"Instantly evaluate a dataset for anomalies without persisting it to the training database.\")\n\n    col3, col4 = st.columns(2)\n    with col3:\n        tenant_id_inf = st.text_input(\"Tenant ID\", \"tenant_1\", key=\"tenant_inf\")\n        greenhouse_id_inf = st.text_input(\"Greenhouse ID\", \"default\", key=\"greenhouse_inf\")\n\n    uploaded_file_inf = st.file_uploader(\"Choose a CSV file for anomaly detection\", type=\"csv\", key=\"file_inf\")\n\n    if st.button(\"Find Anomalies\", type=\"primary\"):\n        if not tenant_id_inf or not greenhouse_id_inf:\n            st.warning(\"Tenant ID and Greenhouse ID cannot be empty.\")\n        elif uploaded_file_inf is not None:\n            with st.spinner(\"Running inference pipeline...\"):\n                files = {\"file\": (uploaded_file_inf.name, uploaded_file_inf.getvalue(), \"text/csv\")}\n                data = {\"tenant_id\": tenant_id_inf, \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id_inf}\n\n                try:\n                    res_inf = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/inference/upload\", files=files, data=data)\n                    res_inf.raise_for_status()\n                    results = res_inf.json()\n\n                    st.success(f\"Processed {results.get('sequences_processed', 0)} sequences. Detected {results.get('anomalies_detected', 0)} anomalies.\")\n\n                    # Visualization\n                    scores = results.get(\"anomaly_scores\", [])\n                    if scores:\n                        df_scores = pd.DataFrame({\n                            \"Sequence Index\": range(len(scores)),\n                            \"Anomaly Score\": scores\n                        })\n\n                        fig = px.line(df_scores, x=\"Sequence Index\", y=\"Anomaly Score\", title=\"Anomaly Scores over Time\")\n                        fig.add_hline(y=ANOMALY_THRESHOLD, line_dash=\"dash\", line_color=\"red\", annotation_text=\"Anomaly Threshold\")\n\n                        st.plotly_chart(fig, use_container_width=True)\n\n                    high_anomalies = results.get(\"high_anomalies\", [])\n                    if high_anomalies:\n                        st.subheader(\"High Anomalies Detected\")\n                        df_high = pd.DataFrame(high_anomalies)\n                        st.dataframe(df_high)\n                    else:\n                        st.info(\"No high anomalies detected in this dataset.\")\n\n                except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n                    st.error(f\"Inference failed: {e}\")\n                    if hasattr(e, 'response') and e.response is not None:\n                        try:\n                            st.json(e.response.json())\n                        except Exception:\n                            st.write(e.response.text)\n        else:\n            st.warning(\"Please upload a CSV file first.\")\n```\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review all the changes made by the ml-engineer, backend-engineer and tech-lead. Ensure the code is correct, follows best practices, and meets the requirements.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: final_review.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it.","thinkingDelta":"","text":"<agent_context>\nSecurity, quality, and guardrails audit. Read files and provide report/ADRs only. No edits to source code.\n\nSPECIFIC REVIEW RESPONSIBILITIES:\n1. Verify guardrails compliance and check for performance, security, and correctness.\n2. File ADR-001 (architecture), ADR-002 (synthetic data), and ADR-003 (modular architecture) under docs/team/ADRs/.\n3. Create docs/review/week1-review.md assessment.\n\nGUARDRAILS:\n# Universal Guardrails\n\n## STOP WORK — never proceed if found\n- Tight coupling between LSTM-VAE and API layer\n- Secrets or API keys hardcoded in source files\n- Model checkpoint saved without metadata (epoch, loss, date, config)\n- Database schema without tenant_id field\n- Test coverage below 80% on critical paths\n- Major design change without ADR in docs/architecture/\n\n## WARN — log and continue\n- Hard-coded thresholds (should be in src/config.py)\n- Missing error handling on external calls\n- Code duplication (3+ identical blocks)\n- Silent failures (bare except, pass)\n\nRED FLAGS:\n# Red Flags — Immediate STOP WORK\n\nIf you see any of these, stop immediately and report to the orchestrator:\n\n1. Any file writing to a path outside its ownership (see CLAUDE.md file ownership table)\n2. Any import of os.system, subprocess with shell=True, or eval()\n3. Any hardcoded password, token, or API key\n4. Any DELETE or DROP in database queries without tenant_id filter\n5. Any model.save() without accompanying metadata JSON\n6. Test file that imports from and modifies implementation files\n7. Circular imports between src/models/ and src/api/\n\n### ACTIVE HANDOVER EXPECTATIONS (WEEK1-FOUNDATION-HANDOVER)\n# Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\nhandover_id: \"week1-foundation\"\nname: \"Week 1-2 Foundation Handover\"\ndescription: \"ML + Backend + DevOps collaborate on foundation\"\n\ncontext: |\n  Week 1-2: Foundation Phase\n\n  ML Engineer is building:\n  - LSTM-VAE model\n  - Synthetic data generator\n  - Training pipeline\n\n  Backend Engineer needs:\n  - Model input/output specifications\n  - Data shape and format\n\n  DevOps Lead needs:\n  - Python dependencies\n  - Memory/compute requirements\n\n  Architect reviews:\n  - Model architecture\n  - Data schema\n  - Integration points\n\ndependencies:\n  - ML provides: Model input/output specs\n  - Backend provides: Schema design\n  - DevOps provides: Compute requirements\n\nhandover_points:\n  day_2:\n    from: \"ml-engineer\"\n    to: \"backend-engineer\"\n    content: \"Model input/output specs\"\n\n  day_3:\n    from: \"backend-engineer\"\n    to: \"devops-lead\"\n    content: \"Python dependencies list\"\n\n  day_4:\n    from: \"all\"\n    to: \"architect\"\n    content: \"Design review and ADRs\"\n</agent_context>\n\n<context_from_previous_agents>\n=== ml-engineer output ===\n# ML Engineer Changes\n\nThis file documents the changes made by the ML Engineer to decouple post-processing logic from the inference API route.\n\n## 1. Created `src/models/postprocessing.py`\n\nA new file was created to house the post-processing logic.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List\n\ndef map_timestamp_to_anomaly(\n    timestamps: pd.Series, reconstruction_error: np.ndarray, threshold: float\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Maps timestamps to detected anomalies based on reconstruction error.\"\"\"\n    anomalies = pd.DataFrame(\n        {\"timestamp\": timestamps, \"reconstruction_error\": reconstruction_error.flatten()}\n    )\n    return anomalies[anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"] > threshold]\n\ndef clip_and_scale_anomalies(\n    anomalies: pd.DataFrame, scaling_factor: float\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Clips anomaly scores and scales them for visualization.\"\"\"\n    anomalies[\"clipped_error\"] = np.clip(anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"], 0, None)\n    anomalies[\"scaled_error\"] = anomalies[\"clipped_error\"] * scaling_factor\n    return anomalies\n\ndef get_high_anomaly_timestamps(\n    anomalies: pd.DataFrame, threshold: float\n) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Filters for high-severity anomalies and returns a list of dictionaries.\"\"\"\n    high_anomalies = anomalies[anomalies[\"reconstruction_error\"] > threshold]\n    return high_anomalies.to_dict(\"records\")\n```\n\n## 2. Updated `src/config.py`\n\nThe configuration file was updated to include new parameters for anomaly detection.\n\n```python\n# =============================================================================\n# Anomaly Detection and Post-Processing\n# =============================================================================\nANOMALY_THRESHOLD: float = 0.8\nANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR: float = 2.0\n```\n\n## 3. Updated `src/api/routes/inference.py`\n\nThe inference route was updated to use the new post-processing functions and configuration values.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Depends\nfrom src.api.schemas.sensor_data import InferenceRequest, InferenceResponse\nfrom src.db.session import get_db\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\nfrom sqlalchemy.future import select\nfrom src.db.models import SensorReading\nfrom src.models.inference import AnomalyDetector\nfrom src.models.model_registry import ModelRegistry\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport numpy as np\nfrom fastapi import UploadFile, File, Form\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\nfrom src.vendors.csv_adapter import CSVAdapter\nfrom src.models.data_utils import preprocess_sequences, normalize_data, SENSOR_RANGES\nfrom src.models.postprocessing import (\n    map_timestamp_to_anomaly,\n    clip_and_scale_anomalies,\n    get_high_anomaly_timestamps,\n)\nfrom src.config import ANOMALY_THRESHOLD, ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\n@router.post(\"/inference\", response_model=InferenceResponse)\nasync def run_inference(\n    request: InferenceRequest,\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    seqs = request.sequences\n    if not seqs:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Empty sequences\")\n\n    # Resolve active model for customer\n    registry = ModelRegistry(db)\n    active_model_info = await registry.get_active_model(request.tenant_id)\n\n    checkpoint_path = None\n    model_id_used = \"baseline_v1\"\n\n    if active_model_info:\n        checkpoint_path = active_model_info[\"checkpoint_path\"]\n        model_id_used = active_model_info[\"model_id\"]\n\n    try:\n        detector = AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=f\"Failed to initialize model: {e}\")\n\n    try:\n        # Expected shape (batch, seq_len, input_dim) -> (batch, 20, 4)\n        np_seqs = [np.array(seq, dtype=np.float32) for seq in seqs]\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(np_seqs)\n        # Scale or clip raw reconstruction errors to [0, 1] range to satisfy Pydantic Schema\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Inference failed: {str(e)}\")\n\n    anomalies_detected = int((batch_scores > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD).sum())\n    high_anomalies = [\n        {\"sequence_index\": i, \"score\": float(s), \"timestamp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\n        for i, s in enumerate(batch_scores)\n        if s > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n    ]\n\n    # Persist scores to the matching database records for this tenant/greenhouse\n    stmt = select(SensorReading).where(\n        SensorReading.tenant_id == request.tenant_id,\n        SensorReading.greenhouse_id == request.greenhouse_id,\n    ).order_by(SensorReading.timestamp.desc()).limit(len(batch_scores))\n\n    result = await db.execute(stmt)\n    records = result.scalars().all()\n\n    # We update records with anomaly scores starting from the matching indices\n    for idx, record in enumerate(reversed(records)):\n        if idx < len(batch_scores):\n            record.anomaly_score = float(batch_scores[idx])\n\n    try:\n        await db.commit()\n    except Exception as e:\n        await db.rollback()\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Failed to persist anomaly scores: {str(e)}\")\n\n    return InferenceResponse(\n        tenant_id=request.tenant_id,\n        greenhouse_id=request.greenhouse_id,\n        sequences_processed=len(seqs),\n        anomalies_detected=anomalies_detected,\n        anomaly_scores=batch_scores.tolist(),\n        high_anomalies=high_anomalies\n    )\n\n\n@router.post(\"/inference/upload\")\nasync def run_inference_from_csv(\n    tenant_id: str = Form(...),\n    greenhouse_id: str = Form(default=\"default\"),\n    file: UploadFile = File(...),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Directly runs inference on an uploaded CSV file without persisting the raw data,\n    returning the anomaly scores and a list of high anomaly items.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not file.filename.endswith(\".csv\"):\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Only CSV files are supported.\")\n\n    content = await file.read()\n\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=\".csv\") as tmp:\n        tmp.write(content)\n        tmp_path = tmp.name\n\n    try:\n        adapter = CSVAdapter({\"filepath\": tmp_path})\n        df = adapter.get_data()\n    except Exception as e:\n        os.unlink(tmp_path)\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=f\"Invalid CSV format: {e}\")\n\n    os.unlink(tmp_path)\n\n    if df.empty:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"Uploaded CSV contains no valid data.\")\n\n    # Extract required columns for inference: temperature, humidity, co2, light\n    try:\n        raw_data = df[[\"temperature\", \"humidity\", \"co2\", \"light\"]].to_numpy()\n    except KeyError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=f\"Missing required columns: {e}\")\n\n    # Normalize data using standard ranges\n    norm_data = normalize_data(raw_data, SENSOR_RANGES)\n\n    try:\n        sequences = preprocess_sequences(norm_data, seq_len=20)\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(e))\n\n    # Resolve active model for customer\n    registry = ModelRegistry(db)\n    active_model_info = await registry.get_active_model(tenant_id)\n\n    checkpoint_path = None\n    if active_model_info:\n        checkpoint_path = active_model_info[\"checkpoint_path\"]\n\n    try:\n        detector = AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=f\"Failed to initialize model: {e}\")\n\n    try:\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(sequences)\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Inference failed: {str(e)}\")\n\n    anomalies_detected = int((batch_scores > ANOMALY_THRESHOLD).sum())\n\n    anomalies_df = map_timestamp_to_anomaly(\n        df[\"timestamp\"], batch_scores, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n    )\n\n    high_anomalies = get_high_anomaly_timestamps(anomalies_df, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD)\n\n    return {\n        \"tenant_id\": tenant_id,\n        \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id,\n        \"sequences_processed\": len(sequences),\n        \"anomalies_detected\": anomalies_detected,\n        \"anomaly_scores\": batch_scores.tolist(),\n        \"high_anomalies\": high_anomalies\n    }\n```\n\n\n=== backend-engineer output ===\n# Backend Optimization Report\n\nThis report outlines the structural enhancements made to the FastAPI backend model inference and upload layers of the AI Agronomist platform. The optimizations guarantee multi-tenant memory safety, robust sliding window math, and model caching with thread-safe limits.\n\n## 🛠️ Summary of Accomplishments\n\n### 1. Memory-Safe Chunked Upload Ingestion (`/api/inference/upload`)\n\n- **Problem**: The old `/api/inference/upload` endpoint performed `file.read()`, holding the entire uploaded file in memory as a giant byte string. It then parsed the database frame all at once via `CSVAdapter.get_data()`. Running model sequences on massive files (e.g., hundreds of megabytes) caused high memory exhaustion and risking Out-of-Memory (OOM) process crashes.\n- **Refactor**:\n  - Implemented streamed buffering to save file bytes in 1MB chunks into a temporary file using `while chunk := await file.read(1024 * 1024):`.\n  - Employed Pandas `read_csv(..., chunksize=5000)` iterator to process the CSV in memory-efficient chunks of 5000 rows.\n  - Verified that each chunk is individually normalized and validated using the `CSVAdapter.normalize` and `CSVAdapter.validate` methods, failing early with a 422 standard HTTP status code if any chunk contains out-of-range sensor measurements, NaNs, or schema infractions.\n  - Ensures that regardless of the file size (from 1KB to multi-gigabytes), the process memory consumption remains tiny and constant.\n\n### 2. Robust Sliding Window Overlap & Timestamp Mapping\n\n- **Problem**: Sliding temporal window math (using `seq_len = 20`) requires groupings of 20 consecutive timestamps. If chunks of size 5000 are processed independently, 19 sequences spanning across chunk boundaries ($seq\\_len - 1$) would be completely discarded. Additionally, mapping anomaly scores to timestamps by aligning lists with different lengths directly results in `ValueError` and index mismatches.\n- **Refactor**:\n  - **Border-Overlap Prepending**: Created a state-carrying buffer `prev_overlap_df` that captures the last `seq_len - 1` (19) rows of each normalized chunk and prepends them onto the next chunk. This guarantees zero border-loss of sequence sliding windows at the chunk transitions.\n  - **Exact Timestamp Mapping**: Mapped each temporal sequence output score $i$ within a chunk back to the exact original timestamp of the end of its window (row $i + seq\\_len - 1$ of the chunk's virtual timeline).\n  - **Safety Bound Checks**: Added boundary safety guards (`if row_idx < len(timestamps):`) and handling for missing/NaT timestamps (resolved to `\"unknown\"`) to completely prevent index out of bounds exceptions. This guarantees 100% robust sequence index mapping.\n\n### 3. Thread-Safe LRU Model Caching\n\n- **Problem**: `AnomalyDetector` models were instantiated from scratch on every incoming request. This resulted in loading heavy PyTorch neural model weights (`LSTMVAE`) over and over, severely dragging request latencies down and filling memory with redundant weights (unbounded leakage).\n- **Refactor**:\n  - Introduced standard library thread-safe `@lru_cache(maxsize=16)` in `src/api/routes/inference.py` wrapping the `AnomalyDetector` factory function:\n    ```python\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=16)\n    def get_cached_detector(checkpoint_path: Optional[str]) -> AnomalyDetector:\n        return AnomalyDetector(checkpoint_path=checkpoint_path)\n    ```\n  - Placed this cached detector factory into both `/api/inference` and `/api/inference/upload` routes. This ensures that when the same customer model or the baseline model is invoked, its weight parameters are re-used instantly, dropping API response time to single-digit milliseconds while bounding memory utilization to at most 16 unique active models.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Modified Files and Code Links\n\nThe modifications are cleanly confined within the backend route and test structures, strictly obeying modular ownership boundaries:\n\n1. **[src/api/routes/inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py)**:\n   - Added `get_cached_detector` with thread-safe `@lru_cache(maxsize=16)` to cache the [AnomalyDetector](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py) instance.\n   - Refactored [run_inference_from_csv](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/api/routes/inference.py) to stream uploaded files chunk-by-chunk and validate/normalize via [CSVAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/csv_adapter.py) iteratively.\n   - Incorporated stateful `prev_overlap_df` logic to retain sliding window continuity.\n2. **[tests/api/test_inference.py](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_inference.py)**:\n   - Added [test_inference_upload_csv](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/tests/api/test_inference.py) verifying that the refactored chunked CSV ingestion endpoint processes sequence batches correctly and maps sequence indices robustly to timestamps.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Code Walkthrough\n\n```python\n# Extract from /api/inference/upload in src/api/routes/inference.py\n@router.post(\"/inference/upload\")\nasync def run_inference_from_csv(\n    tenant_id: str = Form(...),\n    greenhouse_id: str = Form(default=\"default\"),\n    file: UploadFile = File(...),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db)\n):\n    ...\n    # Stream-buffer the uploaded file into a temp file (O(1) memory footprint)\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=\".csv\") as tmp:\n        while chunk := await file.read(1024 * 1024):\n            tmp.write(chunk)\n        tmp_path = tmp.name\n\n    ...\n    # Read CSV in chunks\n    for raw_chunk in pd.read_csv(tmp_path, chunksize=5000):\n        # Normalize and validate chunk independently\n        normalized_chunk = adapter.normalize(raw_chunk)\n        adapter.validate(normalized_chunk)\n\n        # Concat with last chunk's overlap (retaining sliding sequence window math)\n        combined_df = pd.concat([prev_overlap_df, normalized_chunk], ignore_index=True)\n        prev_overlap_df = normalized_chunk.iloc[-(seq_len - 1):].copy()\n\n        ...\n        # Run predictions in mini batch\n        raw_scores = detector.predict_batch(sequences)\n        batch_scores = np.clip(raw_scores / ANOMALY_SCALING_FACTOR, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n        # Safe sliding index timestamp alignment\n        timestamps = combined_df[\"timestamp\"].tolist()\n        for idx, score in enumerate(batch_scores):\n            row_idx = idx + seq_len - 1\n            ts = timestamps[row_idx].isoformat() if row_idx < len(timestamps) else \"unknown\"\n            ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Guardrails & Compliance Check\n\n- **no_tight_coupling**: High compliance. The route layer consumes the unified API contract of [DataSourceAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/base.py) subclass [CSVAdapter](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/vendors/csv_adapter.py) and runs [AnomalyDetector](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/models/inference.py). Both ML and ingest internals are completely decoupled.\n- **canonical_schema**: High compliance. Standard numerical physical ranges ([temp_range](file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/src/config.py#L87-L90), etc.) and column validations are enforced at every individual chunk level.\n- **no_secrets_in_code**: Verified. No credentials or authentication keys are saved inside source code.\n- **test_coverage**: Rigorous integration validations added. Both model cache reuse and large processing pipelines are robustly verified.\n\n\n=== tech-lead output ===\n# Tech Lead Changes\n\nThis file documents the changes made by the Tech Lead to improve the frontend validation and user feedback in the dashboard.\n\n## 1. Updated `src/dashboard/pages/5_upload_operations.py`\n\nThe dashboard page for upload operations was updated to:\n\n- Import `ANOMALY_THRESHOLD` from `src.config` to ensure consistency with the backend.\n- Add frontend validation to ensure that `Tenant ID` and `Greenhouse ID` are not empty before making API calls.\n- Correct the UI notification for model training to reflect its asynchronous nature.\n\n```python\nimport streamlit as st\nimport requests\nimport pandas as pd\nimport plotly.express as px\nfrom src.config import API_URL, ANOMALY_THRESHOLD\n\nst.set_page_config(page_title=\"Upload & Operations\", page_icon=\"📤\", layout=\"wide\")\n\nst.title(\"Data Upload & Model Operations\")\nst.markdown(\"Upload raw sensor data for training or find anomalies instantly using the active model.\")\n\ntab1, tab2 = st.tabs([\"Upload & Train Model\", \"Upload & Find Anomalies\"])\n\nwith tab1:\n    st.header(\"Upload Data & Train Model\")\n    st.write(\"Ingest historical data into the platform and trigger a new model training cycle.\")\n\n    col1, col2 = st.columns(2)\n    with col1:\n        tenant_id_train = st.text_input(\"Tenant ID\", \"tenant_1\", key=\"tenant_train\")\n        greenhouse_id_train = st.text_input(\"Greenhouse ID\", \"default\", key=\"greenhouse_train\")\n\n    uploaded_file_train = st.file_uploader(\"Choose a CSV file for training\", type=\"csv\", key=\"file_train\")\n\n    if st.button(\"Upload & Train\", type=\"primary\"):\n        if not tenant_id_train or not greenhouse_id_train:\n            st.warning(\"Tenant ID and Greenhouse ID cannot be empty.\")\n        elif uploaded_file_train is not None:\n            with st.spinner(\"Uploading data to platform...\"):\n                files = {\"file\": (uploaded_file_train.name, uploaded_file_train.getvalue(), \"text/csv\")}\n                data = {\"tenant_id\": tenant_id_train, \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id_train}\n                try:\n                    res_upload = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/upload\", files=files, data=data)\n                    res_upload.raise_for_status()\n                    st.success(f\"Successfully uploaded {res_upload.json().get('uploaded', 0)} rows.\")\n\n                    st.info(\"Triggering model training pipeline...\")\n                    res_train = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/models/{tenant_id_train}/train\")\n                    res_train.raise_for_status()\n                    st.success(\"Training dispatched in the background.\")\n                    st.json(res_train.json())\n                except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n                    st.error(f\"Operation failed: {e}\")\n                    if hasattr(e, 'response') and e.response is not None:\n                        try:\n                            st.json(e.response.json())\n                        except Exception:\n                            st.write(e.response.text)\n        else:\n            st.warning(\"Please upload a CSV file first.\")\n\nwith tab2:\n    st.header(\"Upload & Find Anomalies\")\n    st.write(\"Instantly evaluate a dataset for anomalies without persisting it to the training database.\")\n\n    col3, col4 = st.columns(2)\n    with col3:\n        tenant_id_inf = st.text_input(\"Tenant ID\", \"tenant_1\", key=\"tenant_inf\")\n        greenhouse_id_inf = st.text_input(\"Greenhouse ID\", \"default\", key=\"greenhouse_inf\")\n\n    uploaded_file_inf = st.file_uploader(\"Choose a CSV file for anomaly detection\", type=\"csv\", key=\"file_inf\")\n\n    if st.button(\"Find Anomalies\", type=\"primary\"):\n        if not tenant_id_inf or not greenhouse_id_inf:\n            st.warning(\"Tenant ID and Greenhouse ID cannot be empty.\")\n        elif uploaded_file_inf is not None:\n            with st.spinner(\"Running inference pipeline...\"):\n                files = {\"file\": (uploaded_file_inf.name, uploaded_file_inf.getvalue(), \"text/csv\")}\n                data = {\"tenant_id\": tenant_id_inf, \"greenhouse_id\": greenhouse_id_inf}\n\n                try:\n                    res_inf = requests.post(f\"{API_URL}/api/inference/upload\", files=files, data=data)\n                    res_inf.raise_for_status()\n                    results = res_inf.json()\n\n                    st.success(f\"Processed {results.get('sequences_processed', 0)} sequences. Detected {results.get('anomalies_detected', 0)} anomalies.\")\n\n                    # Visualization\n                    scores = results.get(\"anomaly_scores\", [])\n                    if scores:\n                        df_scores = pd.DataFrame({\n                            \"Sequence Index\": range(len(scores)),\n                            \"Anomaly Score\": scores\n                        })\n\n                        fig = px.line(df_scores, x=\"Sequence Index\", y=\"Anomaly Score\", title=\"Anomaly Scores over Time\")\n                        fig.add_hline(y=ANOMALY_THRESHOLD, line_dash=\"dash\", line_color=\"red\", annotation_text=\"Anomaly Threshold\")\n\n                        st.plotly_chart(fig, use_container_width=True)\n\n                    high_anomalies = results.get(\"high_anomalies\", [])\n                    if high_anomalies:\n                        st.subheader(\"High Anomalies Detected\")\n                        df_high = pd.DataFrame(high_anomalies)\n                        st.dataframe(df_high)\n                    else:\n                        st.info(\"No high anomalies detected in this dataset.\")\n\n                except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n                    st.error(f\"Inference failed: {e}\")\n                    if hasattr(e, 'response') and e.response is not None:\n                        try:\n                            st.json(e.response.json())\n                        except Exception:\n                            st.write(e.response.text)\n        else:\n            st.warning(\"Please upload a CSV file first.\")\n```\n\n</context_from_previous_agents>\n\nTASK: Review all the changes made by the ml-engineer, backend-engineer and tech-lead. Ensure the code is correct, follows best practices, and meets the requirements.\n\nIMPORTANT: Write your complete output directly to the file: final_review.md\nUse the Write/Create file tools to write the content itself, not Python code that creates it."}}
