2026-06-09 15:08:12,327 - root - INFO - RAW WS MSG: {"seqNum":"39","timestampMicros":"1781014092327478","stepUpdate":{"cascadeId":"d1249288d6b7ecc64a608a0df44e5673","trajectoryId":"d1249288d6b7ecc64a608a0df44e5673","stepIndex":12,"state":"STATE_DONE","source":"SOURCE_MODEL","target":"TARGET_ENVIRONMENT","thinking":"","textDelta":"","thinkingDelta":"","text":"Create ADR-003","editFile":{"filePath":"file:///Users/eugenesidorov/Projects/ai-agronomist/docs/team/ADRs/ADR-003-modular-architecture.md","diffBlock":[{"startLine":0,"endLine":25,"lines":[{"text":"# ADR-003: Modular Architecture","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"## Status","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"Proposed","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"# ADR-003: Modular and Decoupled Service Architecture","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Date**: 2026-06-09","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Status**: Accepted","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Context","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"The AI Agronomist platform is a complex system with multiple components, including a frontend, a backend, and a machine learning pipeline. To ensure the long-term maintainability and scalability of the platform, it is important to adopt a modular architecture that promotes loose coupling and high cohesion.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"The platform is designed to evolve. A monolithic architecture would hinder our ability to scale, innovate, and maintain separate parts of the system. We need an architecture that allows for independent development, deployment, and scaling of different components, such as the inference API, the data processing pipeline, and the user-facing dashboard.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Decision","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"We will adopt a modular architecture based on the following principles:","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Separation of Concerns:** Each module should have a single, well-defined responsibility.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Loose Coupling:** Modules should be independent of each other and should communicate through well-defined interfaces.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **High Cohesion:** The elements within a module should be closely related and should work together to achieve a common goal.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"We will implement a modular service-oriented architecture, where each major functional area is a distinct, containerized service. The key principles are:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Separation of Concerns**: Each service has a single, well-defined responsibility. For example, the `api` service handles HTTP requests, the `models` service manages machine learning models, and the `db` service is responsible for data persistence.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **API-Based Communication**: Services communicate via well-defined, versioned RESTful APIs. This decouples the services and allows them to be developed and updated independently.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Containerization**: Each service will be packaged as a Docker container, simplifying deployment and ensuring consistency across environments.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"## Consequences","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"},{"text":"The adoption of a modular architecture will have the following consequences:","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Improved Maintainability:** The modular architecture will make it easier to maintain and update the platform.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Improved Scalability:** The modular architecture will make it easier to scale the platform to meet the needs of a growing user base.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"- **Improved Testability:** The modular architecture will make it easier to test the individual components of the platform.","action":"LINE_ACTION_DELETE"},{"text":"**Pros**:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Agility**: Teams can develop, test, and deploy their services independently, leading to faster development cycles.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Scalability**: Each service can be scaled independently based on its specific resource requirements.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Resilience**: The failure of one service is less likely to impact the entire system.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Technology Diversity**: Different services can be implemented using different technologies, as long as they adhere to the API contracts.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"**Cons**:","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Operational Complexity**: Managing a distributed system of services is more complex than managing a monolith.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Network Latency**: Communication between services can introduce network latency.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"- **Data Consistency**: Ensuring data consistency across multiple services can be challenging.","action":"LINE_ACTION_INSERT"},{"text":"","action":"LINE_ACTION_NONE"}]}]}}}
